(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
What Makes Wolfram QuantumFramework Unique: A Verified Showcase\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"b3162b95-5fa8-4cb6-83ee-569386404830"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Wolfram QuantumFramework is a quantum laboratory built into the Wolfram \
Language. The objects of quantum theory, states, operators, channels, \
measurements, circuits, are exact symbolic or numeric expressions: they can \
carry free parameters, compose with one another in closed form, and answer \
questions about themselves through one uniform interface. A computation here \
typically ends in a formula, the propagator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "222a2713-7400-4d76-a17d-69573bd58de1"],
 " of a time-dependent Hamiltonian, an optimization landscape you can \
differentiate, an entanglement entropy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38eccc68-d752-4dac-a397-44dc77ff9c30"],
 " you can solve, rather than a table of numbers, though a fully numeric \
workflow is equally supported. The same objects run in any finite dimension, \
qubits, qutrits, spin-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e52ebb7-d865-42e1-81c9-c52b453e1315"],
 " multiplets, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["N", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "91827893-1e6e-4f79-aa10-010fa44e0a91"],
 "-level systems, and they reach outward as well, to OpenQASM, to device \
transpilation, to real quantum hardware. It is most useful when the goal is \
insight rather than a number: a closed form, an exact threshold, a verified \
physical statement. These are not estimates that tighten with more shots or a \
finer grid; they are exact, so where a numeric run or a finite measurement \
returns a value, QF returns the closed form, the exact integer, or the \
algebraic root that the value only approximates."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7266950f-82b7-4624-9a20-d0da1514e0b2"],

Cell["\<\
This document makes that concrete as seven claims, each developed through \
worked examples:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"83428ca6-c7ef-46e8-b254-4cff563293bd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Symbolic-first, exact algebra by default.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Time-dependent Hamiltonians solved to closed-form propagators, an exact \
QAOA landscape, a many-body entanglement entropy as a formula in time."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"e275d42d-5470-4a31-8df6-81799c3b43d8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["One object model spans all of quantum theory.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Channels, POVMs, bosonic Fock space, and phase-space quasi-probabilities \
are the same kind of object as a gate; a master equation solves symbolically \
for every state and every rate at once; every object carries its own basis; \
the model runs in any finite dimension, from a spin-1 qutrit to a five-site \
ring; and it closes with a full state-tomography loop."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"b0e2cd16-7e67-4425-88dc-9a1f9bbb0eb7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Measurement records are quantum wires.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A measurement appends a pointer qudit instead of collapsing the state, so \
feedforward is a controlled gate on a record: teleportation carries its \
classical channel as a quantum wire, a coherent error is digitized and \
corrected at codeword fidelity exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a0364f1-ee24-4492-a858-2a71e2128757"],
 ", and a measurement can be run in reverse."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"8b11a3cc-49c4-4ac0-aaaf-0a852906db8a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["One object model, three computational engines.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The same circuit runs as exact state-vector algebra, as a steered \
tensor-network contraction, or as a compiled stabilizer tableau that \
represents a thousand-qubit state, and the representations convert into one \
another exactly."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"f2a54385-3296-4703-b478-8caca115ff6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A quantum object is an ordinary Wolfram Language expression.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Native functions operate on the object: ",
 Cell[BoxData["Exp"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "074f04d4-ba6d-45dd-bde2-6916ac59c5d8"],
 " exponentiates a generator into a propagator, ",
 Cell[BoxData["D"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dea4df4f-a2b0-446b-8217-2aea9483b55a"],
 " differentiates a gate into another operator, ",
 Cell[BoxData["Plus"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ab8faf1-f0e6-421e-b587-796df603e87f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["Commutator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08c9971d-30d4-4831-8717-db0586543d30"],
 " build a Hamiltonian, and the closed forms they yield pass directly into \
solvers."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"4394ee10-7184-4111-96fe-5a7b64e60bbc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Every object draws itself.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Bloch spheres, amplitude charts that carry the phases, measurement \
histograms, circuit diagrams, and the tensor network behind a circuit, each a \
one-call property of the object it depicts."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"2e6867a5-bed5-486e-8b5b-b368deb17090"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["An interoperability hub, down to real hardware.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " OpenQASM in and out natively; transpilation to a device target; submission \
to a real QPU, with IBM as the worked example."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"3bf168dc-3e0f-492b-b9d9-5ce42af9c92b"],

Cell["\<\
The claims build on one another, from symbolic objects to real hardware, so \
we begin with the symbolic algebra that the others rely on.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f8a98441-c8ea-4d80-b39a-5992b7accacb"],

Cell["Claim 1: Symbolic-first, exact algebra by default", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5251b42f-1602-4453-af41-efe5031d1009"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Key feature:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " symbolic algebra runs through the entire object model, not a single \
function. The basic objects, a state (",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8450884c-8baf-48e9-8631-dc10920679d7"],
 "), a Hamiltonian (",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bbf994f2-9d98-4d37-81ef-508071296eaf"],
 "), its time evolution (",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76e1c71c-f75c-4437-9265-98141471571c"],
 "), and a circuit (",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumCircuitOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cf4716e6-12ca-4999-bda4-127a3473d21f"],
 "), are each fully symbolic and compose into exact closed-form results. They \
are treated here in that order, beginning with the simplest: a state whose \
amplitudes are symbols."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5c8e2769-cca5-4004-8951-b11114d38025"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Closest competitor.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " An actively-maintained third-party symbolic-quantum Mathematica package \
matches the symbolic gate algebra, the symbolic Lindblad master equation, and \
the symbolic entropy shown here. What remains distinctive is the closed-form \
time-ordered propagator returned from a Hamiltonian object, expressed through \
parabolic-cylinder and Kummer functions that SymPy and every Julia package \
cannot represent at all."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4df2ff06-6122-4c24-a7da-0e65f1adf506"],

Cell["A symbolic state", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"bc2e5dc3-69d9-4462-b182-7d3e96068c4e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f81466d-8447-43e9-8beb-ce2151305a18"],
 " can carry free symbols. The object to build is the general qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{"i", "\[Beta]"}], "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
     TemplateBox[{"1"},
      "Ket"]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d14c432-a9c7-4a3f-88f3-0f37f8134226"],
 ": not one state but the whole two-parameter family at once. Build it:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"17daa2cc-0737-4d95-9510-5f018e29f936"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Alpha]", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Alpha]", "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[Beta]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"aa469316-7338-46e6-bc68-e13b1b8df4db"],

Cell["\<\
The object carries both amplitudes as symbols. Read them back as a plain \
vector:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1dc526f6-bd87-4c0a-943e-a74953759d57"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "Normal"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"09fc5ad7-339e-48fe-867f-8bf66070cf71"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The amplitudes return exactly as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{"i", "\[Beta]"}], "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a52d461b-e6a7-4d46-ac96-fccc661bf6ad"],
 ", symbols intact."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1a96e130-f8f4-46b7-8d82-f533cec97e32"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same object reports its exact Bloch geometry, the expectation triple ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "=", 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "604472ea-2f28-4c4f-90d3-e1c00752bb08"],
 " that places the qubit on the unit sphere (",
 Cell[BoxData["ComplexExpand"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b2b92b31-fc74-4c7b-ae15-11a684e020a3"],
 " treats ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d513e5a-83a5-4ddd-b5e7-e131508372d8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a5735fc-41fb-4eac-a875-917c069527a2"],
 " as real):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"455f0095-ff45-45b5-870c-f8938436e9ac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<BlochVector\>\"", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
   "ComplexExpand"}], " ", "//", " ", "FullSimplify"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"f834d94d-9216-4621-8e37-fd5827704fe2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Bloch vector returns exactly as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9021013d-1703-427a-b244-fc61cda50841"],
 ": the full geometry as functions of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "144eddcd-a001-4274-a133-7d5b4d2e830d"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "44ec8d8b-bd46-4bc9-aee4-6720654e4c89"],
 ", without committing to numbers."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c970df6c-6f55-4f06-902b-55d30261e762"],

Cell["A time-dependent symbolic Hamiltonian", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"e22a92b7-185a-4605-8ac7-65b52c78bce5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Hamiltonians need not be static. The following is a spin-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f77dd55-416e-4a99-b9c7-0c9b43a3c9a8"],
 " in a magnetic field that rotates in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "y"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ca5c8a5-abd6-4117-a297-afd944a6862e"],
 "-plane at frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2dfdfd39-bee3-4401-8709-c771f5ccdb96"],
 ", on top of a static ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b12f50b2-8621-4883-adb3-887d9e7fcefc"],
 "-field, the standard model of magnetic resonance and of a driven qubit:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01ffabc9-6bd6-463c-a432-d6d8496b78f5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"], "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "+", 
   FractionBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"51e9ecb0-9610-4d15-\
a4f6-14b0f3db2d42"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is explicitly time-dependent, built as a function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"h", "[", "t", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "890afb0f-301e-4403-ac76-3cdb9de01b61"],
 " whose operator carries the time ",
 Cell[BoxData["t"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e218188b-fd7f-49aa-96f6-208fdb54edc7"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9761a75c-7633-4c35-8013-ee1471caa410"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "h", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"h", "[", "t_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", "/", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", 
   "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Y\>\"", "]"}]}]}], 
     ")"}]}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a782c250-e84d-4995-9785-1c768ef3bb3e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Because the field direction rotates, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aa0db903-2b8b-4e82-8fa1-9e841a07ae0c"],
 " does not commute with itself at different times, so the propagator is not \
simply ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Integral]",
     FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7b2075b-9646-45a0-a328-77a5c0d34a6d"],
 "; it requires genuine time-ordering. Check the non-commutativity directly, \
applying ",
 Cell[BoxData["Commutator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "248d7ed4-7b4d-4fd8-bf57-f088ac07462e"],
 " to the two operator objects ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d3c0e84f-a056-43fd-92d8-5cf6433c5936"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31fe2ea9-cc61-4ce8-8d0c-0ab69ea52c34"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b7851dfa-e5cf-4929-8692-10d31e97979c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Commutator", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"h", "[", "t1", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"h", "[", "t2", "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], 
   " ", "//", " ", "Normal"}], " ", "//", " ", "FullSimplify"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2d203f19-16c1-44bf-ac49-d9eac88c7f81"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The commutator is nonzero, with diagonal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[MinusPlus]", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["[",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e5b4496e-b1b3-47d4-b3f3-f23e7b369ded"],
 ": the evolution genuinely requires time-ordering and does not reduce to a \
static problem."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c1e24faa-a318-4e49-b94b-d83df19a4551"],

Cell["Its propagator, in closed form", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"814478ca-a810-45af-aff0-7f795b8c8c18"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d18888d-e8e2-4ba7-ae7d-6393c9e3bc9c"],
 " is QF's single entry point for time evolution: it propagates a state \
forward or returns the propagator itself, under closed-system (Schrodinger) \
or open-system (Lindblad) dynamics, numerically or, when the inputs carry \
symbols, in closed form. Given the Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"h", "[", "t", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f7ef1901-2bec-4176-a753-3df54c5fd2d4"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["None"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "197aa530-7db9-4e9f-bf7c-04a889325b64"],
 " in place of an initial state, and the time variable ",
 Cell[BoxData["t"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ab96310-ffd2-40e0-99db-ea7ac55ba22c"],
 ", it returns the propagator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "93ab4552-9db4-4180-a772-579d680d4aa8"],
 " solving ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], " ", 
   SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["U", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "055019e6-9a19-468d-9b6d-e880d0cac0a1"],
 ". (Verified here: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "176c430f-ce40-4653-9087-ac765b4f14c5"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31a83b43-57b1-4d6c-af81-b68cf417d6e4"],
 " exactly.)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56230822-14b6-453f-9b60-6f3930052e9f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"urot", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"h", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", "None", ",", " ", "t"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6546caf9-0377-4e5b-b66c-4c7eee2db816"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Simplify its matrix under real parameters and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f7d0ed1-ac81-4879-b2e0-26768a0313bc"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"77c160d8-862d-42c0-a17e-52d9a27b3a15"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Assuming", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"t", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
     RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
       RowBox[{"urot", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}], " ", "//", " ", "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6839d729-6d2b-40e0-bdcf-3dd78e623761"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The matrix returns exactly as the lab-frame Rabi propagator, written here \
with the detuning ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[Congruent]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "191c40e6-d35f-4e52-a7bc-ca29fda47b4b"],
 " and the generalized Rabi frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "\[Congruent]", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "2"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01442be4-be13-4b1e-82df-c206e102f800"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c8840cb9-0422-42d4-adbb-c1b7690e7623"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "(", GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", "(", 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["cos",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
        FractionBox[
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
           StyleBox["R", "TI"]], 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "2"], "+", 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
        FractionBox[
         StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
         SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
          StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], 
        StyleBox["sin",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
        FractionBox[
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
           StyleBox["R", "TI"]], 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "2"]}], ")"}], 
      RowBox[{"-", " ", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], " ", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], " ", 
       FractionBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
         StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], 
       StyleBox["sin",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
          StyleBox["R", "TI"]], 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "2"]}]},
     {
      RowBox[{"-", " ", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], " ", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], " ", 
       FractionBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
        SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
         StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], 
       StyleBox["sin",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
          StyleBox["R", "TI"]], 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "2"]}], 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", "(", 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["cos",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
        FractionBox[
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
           StyleBox["R", "TI"]], 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "2"], "-", 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
        FractionBox[
         StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
         SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
          StyleBox["R", "TI"]]], 
        StyleBox["sin",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
        FractionBox[
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
           StyleBox["R", "TI"]], 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "2"]}], ")"}]}
    }], ")"}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"e1d0dc56-b7ac-4e5e-\
9838-414362f07800"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"\[MinusPlus]", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b5568947-cb2b-47a9-b55d-5e7045bf8def"],
 " factors are the rotating-frame phases, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["cos",
   FontSlant->"Plain"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "605bfb81-bda4-4793-ae32-0feb8f2b6a9e"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["sin",
   FontSlant->"Plain"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d0da76-cc93-41f2-a84c-b4069bfae4a2"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9f959f66-dd21-4858-8300-d98dbc4ab7ae"],
 " are the dressed-state oscillations. The quantity of physical interest is \
the transition probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       TemplateBox[{"1"},
        "Bra"], 
       StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
       TemplateBox[{"0"},
        "Ket"]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4362578a-d63f-4459-8eec-ed010a330f4a"],
 ". Take the lower-left matrix entry, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "\[Rule]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "af0a216f-19b0-4a9c-8c9b-5dbfc74e46aa"],
 " amplitude:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d9c82fdd-fb69-4153-91ca-5c939172747a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"amp", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"urot", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0a680e6c-aac0-4a44-a0f9-75840a64b35c"],

Cell["\<\
Then square its magnitude under the same real-parameter assumptions:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4a812112-1af4-447e-b1ea-e75cb0959452"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Assuming", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"t", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "amp", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ec5172da-bb50-4e02-ba37-470ca2d99254"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is the textbook Rabi formula, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"0", "\[Rule]", "1"}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "2"]}]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "2"]}]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11f69c0e-ea7f-4b53-9162-1c79f97603d9"],
 ". On resonance (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f11cc2a-b46c-4a13-a68e-e7c94897d323"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20be415e-a217-49e5-99bc-ae6967ba7103"],
 ") this is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "84176aba-a077-442d-a454-f4bc4c67ca71"],
 ": complete Rabi flopping between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12d4f9ed-bd09-4893-981c-e2989b98a66c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3cd297d8-028e-4ef3-8873-2cad073a467e"],
 ". The oscillation rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "2"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ac082a85-8f2b-4bd6-8502-8e1843fa718a"],
 " is the generalized Rabi frequency, the dressed-state gap in the rotating \
frame, here recovered as a closed-form function of the drive detuning and \
strength."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1a7cf8b6-e008-4d7c-9739-4385cb785494"],

Cell["When the closed form needs special functions: Landau-Zener", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"e410d020-866b-4d40-a249-27e2d38ecef3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The rotating-field propagator was elementary, but symbolic evolution is not \
limited to elementary functions. Sweep the energy bias linearly through an \
avoided crossing at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["v", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5abb6f62-6ac7-4c84-b625-5aaac58e0d7a"],
 " with a constant gap ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalDelta]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b88e021d-8503-429d-ab2a-9824e3ce688c"],
 ": the Landau-Zener model ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"v", "t"}], "TI"], "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "+", 
   FractionBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c0dbc69-909e-402b-9a4d-9e5e236615b7"],
 ", which asks whether a system swept through a level crossing stays in its \
energy branch or crosses the gap. It is again time-dependent and \
non-commuting:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"af840aac-c80c-42ee-8f68-3b4dfebe7de1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hlz", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"v", " ", 
    RowBox[{"t", "/", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "/", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[10]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"24cdfad1-e76e-46d9-a355-55a77c6f64f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ask ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "079ba34c-b9a6-4aa3-bd66-5b6bd92e42f9"],
 " for the propagator:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7464b0b6-86b7-47b9-811c-d44a989a76a3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ulz", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{"hlz", ",", " ", "None", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[11]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e643f9a9-cb1f-40a7-b574-99cd85df688f"],

Cell["Then simplify its full matrix:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5e738726-0acf-489b-963c-7814c79d658a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lzmat", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ulz", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[12]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"9f261f5e-f82f-41ce-a6ad-be535779838c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The matrix is a genuine special-function object. Its first entry alone \
reads ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], "/", "4"}]], 
     SubscriptBox[" ", "1"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["F", "TI"], "1"], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["(",
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
       SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "2"]}], 
      RowBox[{"8", 
       StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]]}], ";", " ", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], "2"], " ", 
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8c992f52-8255-4a21-9bb3-6e20644aeaad"],
 ", and across the four entries the Kummer function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["", "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], "1"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0be3a52f-1a3a-48f3-80c3-bcec4ce5d694"],
 ", fractional-order Hermite functions, and parabolic cylinder functions ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fdda56f3-aad7-4116-8f17-61338c14cb1b"],
 " appear together, with ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalGamma]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ae54018-11db-4af6-a6f4-88e7b435b2fd"],
 "-function coefficients, the single dimensionless ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e126cab-43cf-487b-83ff-f982c8d6bb46"],
 " setting every index and phase. These are one family in several forms: each \
solves the same Weber equation, shown here as the symbolic solver returned \
it. The matrix is a valid propagator (numerically ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "de0c81d3-1bcb-4cbd-939c-2d959baa151e"],
 ", it solves the Schrodinger equation, and it is unitary), and at long times \
its asymptotics reduce to the Landau-Zener transition probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "\[Pi]", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "2"], "/", "2", 
     StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d2d1c02d-214c-4dd7-9696-596dd2c6492e"],
 ". Symbolic evolution here reaches beyond elementary functions to the \
special-function solution the physics requires."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"819778a2-2894-4e02-85e7-a05ddb487759"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Having the whole propagator, not just its asymptote, is clearest in a plot. \
First convert the special-function matrix into a numeric parametric operator: \
fix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["v", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74eeb980-5ffa-4dea-84b7-986bb6b7d57a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["g", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1707c5e9-0906-4bcb-bb04-7fa037ff8528"],
 ", so a single dimensionless parameter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dfe33349-d83d-4282-b517-67013ac66a46"],
 " sets the adiabaticity, and declare ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["g", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03d5f81f-00b0-4ad9-9aa5-ecdd27d6abe6"],
 " and the time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e8ce4a2-0649-4d22-95bf-d62f155cefda"],
 " as parameters:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a0190c25-5cd7-40bc-8d89-e5d7f7cb05bc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"op", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"N", "@", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"lzmat", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"v", " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "g", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "t"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[13]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ac047757-cbc9-44a7-a390-635a5f59fbc7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"op", "[", 
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "400520c2-2b7b-4914-b7e5-bd6c3d2ac091"],
 " is the Landau-Zener propagator at adiabaticity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["g", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9daeb4b1-2295-402d-92c7-de975b520995"],
 " and time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d64badc2-6fb4-455e-9f7e-5e0f59d72817"],
 ", evaluated numerically on demand."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00afba52-08ff-40d7-aa32-af603e8249a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The survival is the probability of staying in the diabatic ground state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "95e93d4b-7705-4582-8a1c-b863934f993c"],
 " across the sweep. Propagate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ee0b15f0-4ad0-4c2f-a09e-7264e5801e95"],
 " from well before the crossing at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "-", "10"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56a91962-a2e8-443d-a3a5-7d72a992fc22"],
 " to time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "95550043-f300-4650-b08d-ecf75fb0fa47"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["op",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["op",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "878dea6b-ce1d-4ce3-aeb0-601263176c4e"],
 ", and read off ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      TemplateBox[{"0", 
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
          StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
       "BraKet"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "acc54a46-51b1-459d-b2dc-83980deab25f"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7899080c-015f-48ac-95f4-0bbe9666676d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "survival", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"survival", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"op", "[", 
          RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
        "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], 
           "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], "@", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"op", "[", 
            RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "[", "c", "]"}]}], ")"}], 
        "[", "\"\<Scalar\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[14]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c42d08f1-86ad-47d8-b9bd-65327c529766"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"survival", "[", 
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1148bdb2-a5a7-4fd4-b829-0527093c96c1"],
 " is now a closed-form function of adiabaticity and time, assembled entirely \
by composing QF objects, without a differential solver."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9ed3dc27-085e-4e9d-8fe3-58fc1f73a3ca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Take three regimes: a fast (diabatic) sweep, an intermediate one, and a \
slow (adiabatic) sweep, set by the single ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57c94b7e-c033-4dec-85c3-51abcb2cbfcb"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"faeb1cc9-ee55-43df-aed1-be23e9e45e5d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ratios", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0.1", ",", " ", "0.6", ",", " ", "1.6"}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[15]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"9c6b3b94-f958-48b5-a117-b2da43433936"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plot the survival across the crossing for each, with the asymptotic \
Landau-Zener formula ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "\[Pi]", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "2"], "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e6088e4-9cca-4331-880b-c72120476a1d"],
 " drawn as dashed lines:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e2a0a5cc-ffba-4417-beb6-514c0ef5b5bc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Evaluate", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"survival", "[", 
       RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "ratios"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"-", "10"}], ",", " ", "10"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time  t  (avoided crossing at t = 0)\>\"", ",", "\n", 
      "        ", "\"\<Survival  |\[LeftAngleBracket]0|\[Psi](t)\
\[RightAngleBracket]|^2\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Placed", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<\[CapitalDelta]\.b2/v = 0.1  (diabatic)\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<0.6  (intermediate)\>\"", ",", "\n", 
        "    ", "\"\<1.6  (adiabatic)\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0.78", ",", " ", "0.6"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sequence", " ", "@@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "10"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"-", "Pi"}], " ", 
                 RowBox[{"#", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"10", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"-", "Pi"}], " ", 
                 RowBox[{"#", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], 
          " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "ratios"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}], ",", " ", "None"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[16]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"32f6f88c-6baa-4790-87ad-5350a1da2a74"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The dashed lines are the textbook asymptotic value; the solid curves are \
the exact survival from the special-function propagator. Each drops through \
the crossing at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7234761-a38c-4a1f-9f79-55d76f965923"],
 " and then oscillates about its asymptote with a slowly decaying envelope, \
the Landau-Zener-St\[UDoubleDot]ckelberg oscillations carried by the \
parabolic cylinder functions, which the asymptotic formula does not show. The \
asymptotic result is the long-time average of the exact answer, and the \
single ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["v", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5a5fc218-37ed-4084-98fb-c33a43a429af"],
 " orders the whole family: a fast (diabatic) sweep barely dips and stays in \
its branch, a slow (adiabatic) sweep transfers almost completely. The closed \
form gives the entire time-resolved crossing, oscillations included, where \
the asymptotic formula gives only the final number."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d349dca8-a9a5-4b00-8fee-cfe6678ae8cb"],

Cell["A parametric circuit: QAOA, built entirely from a graph", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"8ece0bc2-4704-4761-a8f2-fdab644a1175"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "QAOA is the canonical parametric circuit for optimization: one layer \
alternates a cost unitary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["C", "TI"]]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0409f3c0-2289-4b34-aff3-8d50525ae066"],
 " with a mixer ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b381a432-1aff-428a-8f3a-4fda8bc7fdc6"],
 ", and the two angles are tuned to maximize a classical objective. The \
objective here is MaxCut: color the vertices of a graph with two colors ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e732b94-985c-4968-9bf3-296ec5a2a0fe"],
 " so that as many edges as possible join different colors, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox[
    StyleBox["max",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["s", "TI"], " ", "\[Element]", " ", "{", "\[PlusMinus]", "1", 
     SuperscriptBox["}", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}],
    LimitsPositioning->False], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Element]", 
     StyleBox["E", "TI"]}],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f6c0b352-4c88-4378-842f-28cd0e73fad3"],
 ". Everything below is derived from the problem graph, so nothing is \
hardcoded. Take the complete graph on four vertices, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "763418da-646a-4b19-b6b7-1dabb7f155ae"],
 ", a frustrated instance in which not all six edges can be cut:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4e5357c2-f2b0-42dd-82bc-4b34e12fb791"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"graph", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"CompleteGraph", "[", "4", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[17]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"17eaece5-7834-4491-aba4-adbebdfc393c"],

Cell["\<\
Read off the classical optimum, its best two-coloring of the vertices:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0363d053-c29b-484d-8c8e-d6828fa1faef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FindMaximumCut", "[", "graph", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[18]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"bd48e567-df2e-42e1-b95b-b655716d74c7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The classical answer is a cut of ",
 Cell[BoxData["4"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bc3e2e6f-ad48-4c76-bcf3-c385223289f3"],
 " of the ",
 Cell[BoxData["6"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b0d79ede-eece-456d-92c7-f5a254cb22e4"],
 " edges, splitting the four vertices into two pairs. Record the vertex count \
for reuse:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c3977423-1b13-4aaf-8a5c-11039bd60e43"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"VertexCount", "[", "graph", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[19]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"fbee075a-5a5f-4117-9fcf-722cf2bb082a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The MaxCut cost Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "653944e0-f88f-4f64-bfa1-33c8aad89cb6"],
 " is assembled straight from the edge list, one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d25d69b-8225-483a-9ea8-68befc37b468"],
 " term per edge, and carries a label that will name its block in the diagram \
below:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7210d499-6f93-4a50-87e0-b3a9b096d610"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hcost", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"id", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
           RowBox[{"StringJoin", "[", 
            RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
             RowBox[{"\"\<I\>\"", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
          "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"id", " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"\"\<ZZ\>\"", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}], " ", 
          "&"}], ")"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"List", " ", "@@@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"EdgeList", "[", "graph", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
    ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Label\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Hamiltonian\>\""}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[20]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1b4f34ad-0bc1-4d86-a131-e94cc39f70e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Change ",
 Cell[BoxData["graph"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "016a8430-04f9-48aa-9950-2677582f365a"],
 " and this operator adapts to any graph."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"335e99e7-424c-4020-ab1e-56ed6e88a846"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ansatz is built one labeled piece at a time. State prep puts every \
qubit in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a1660c9d-b008-4d6c-b57c-f7634891373c"],
 ", an equal superposition over all cuts:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f85736ca-abd4-4774-8f59-9b99b66ee879"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"stateprep", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"StringJoin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<0\>\"", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", "n", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Label\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Prep\>\""}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[21]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"bf9d4864-a34d-4c19-8aa7-b3789f8777b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The cost layer applies one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75e96cb7-b250-4af7-9587-55cbe742cfa2"],
 " rotation per edge, carrying the angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23c973e9-d75a-418b-ba2e-7708fefc1c02"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e4bd6be2-990f-4ccb-92fc-bc0e2cfc4008"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qcost", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<R\>\"", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", ",", " ", "\"\<ZZ\>\""}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
        "#"}], " ", "&"}], ")"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"List", " ", "@@@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"EdgeList", "[", "graph", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "\[Gamma]", "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Label\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Cost\>\""}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[22]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a1de35d9-60b6-45ca-a7a2-fb4689ff6e63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The mixer applies an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fc22365f-9496-4523-964d-02eb30e3b421"],
 " to every vertex:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4fe1cf02-d71a-4cbc-ba97-3124f5e917f7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mixer", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<RX\>\"", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"VertexList", "[", "graph", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "\[Theta]", "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Label\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Mixer\>\""}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[23]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1e0a0c2a-bfd1-4e1f-ac97-2307d1443265"],

Cell["Compose the three into one parametric layer:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"83d3ac98-adfb-425f-94c5-90cafbf4aec0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"oneLayer", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"stateprep", ",", " ", "qcost", ",", " ", "mixer"}], "}"}], ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[24]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e61a5399-e54d-4f5e-888d-4fa7847fb901"],

Cell["No qubit index was written by hand.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"50bdae90-b14c-47aa-bf09-cdf2a4fc7fd4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The cost landscape is the expectation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Bra"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"]], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e226fd2e-2744-4766-a530-f130a1cd0bee"],
 ", and here QF uses a feature worth stating explicitly: a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumCircuitOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9ecef3e4-250d-41d5-a9d0-9daecda5919e"],
 " can hold states as elements. Composing the prep circuit (the ket), the \
operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["C", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b9a6e692-c280-4e4a-b338-64e5411ab265"],
 ", and the prep circuit's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66f9ec57-55b8-49ba-bd83-32186363030d"],
 " (the bra) builds ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Bra"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"]], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43934213-72a8-4917-ac80-f3687b257da0"],
 " as a single object:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"494736c8-536b-4f78-b0ef-7f8f7f0d1b80"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"meanvalue", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"oneLayer", " ", "/*", " ", "hcost", " ", "/*", " ", 
    RowBox[{"oneLayer", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[25]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"48bfdeec-ff3d-4604-8ae7-6fd1174c7884"],

Cell["That object draws itself:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"95a31a24-fa88-47f4-ba38-68d7e06885af"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"meanvalue", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[26]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6ef5e63d-dc52-406b-9090-a74b670e902f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The diagram shows the bra-ket structure block by block: the labeled ",
 Cell[BoxData["Prep"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cab045b-e5c4-4ae2-8a84-d5d09976c477"],
 "/",
 Cell[BoxData["Cost"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "df1f1b8f-1a71-4386-ad13-25299bd3003f"],
 "/",
 Cell[BoxData["Mixer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "86927c76-a5b2-4aa7-963f-16e2267a9b01"],
 " layer, the ",
 Cell[BoxData["Hamiltonian"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d28d602e-4d4f-40f4-be6b-a86ba57b7ad1"],
 " in the middle, and the daggered layer mirrored on the right. Calling the \
same object with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"[", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Scalar\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "629ccc1b-74ce-4216-abf3-f9477a81e249"],
 " returns the number, with no manual inner product:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6e2a2bea-5569-4fa4-8b55-04029c25982a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"landscape", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"meanvalue", "[", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Scalar\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", ",", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}],
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[27]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"8d68bfec-345d-481c-959d-7e6372efc4a4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The exact QAOA energy landscape returns as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   FractionBox["3", "8"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], "7", "+", 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "+", "2", 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "4", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "-", "8", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "18b4ff7f-52d4-4a7d-af10-36e4d9cafb78"],
 ", a closed form in the two angles."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2244c7aa-0a75-4f09-95a3-8f1fbb743e02"],

Cell["\<\
Because the landscape is a formula, the whole optimization problem can be \
looked at before it is solved. Plot the surface over a full period of both \
angles:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a311c529-9711-4efc-8fd2-f2e194f19c98"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot3D", "[", 
  RowBox[{"landscape", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Pi]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Pi]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[Gamma]\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Theta]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<cost\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<TemperatureMap\>\""}], ",", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotPoints", " ", "->", " ", "50"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[28]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"52c9ca5e-8f94-453f-8d79-7740d783c818"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The surface is the entire variational problem: smooth, with period ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b37e82f-41eb-4537-b35b-84efc5464170"],
 " in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "063b62dd-27dd-46a8-9b19-318f9cdf2a58"],
 " but ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e05b6a74-8adc-4375-a344-95ec0fc0341b"],
 " in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eb57cbe7-6e27-4d68-855c-a155a3689eb5"],
 " (the cost angle enters through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e59e05b4-84f8-4933-ac4a-9124b5ae90e2"],
 ", not only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c3fb3a0f-fe59-4ced-b11f-7abf0d53b071"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26bf4e96-e816-435b-802d-15a3a705c1a8"],
 " needs a full ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f308e381-0a79-4834-bc2d-50ad2c3e0daa"],
 " to repeat), and flat at the value ",
 Cell[BoxData["3"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7eec9198-488e-4c6a-be72-a9737bf97b66"],
 " along the line ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21337fac-5599-4418-bc80-6ba015452077"],
 ", where the cost layer is inactive and the equal superposition cuts ",
 Cell[BoxData["3"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f390ea5b-b47b-4b04-b666-fa5e419fe1ee"],
 " of the ",
 Cell[BoxData["6"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2afe4002-a641-4879-8062-59a1bc099204"],
 " edges on average. What an experiment estimates point by point, with shot \
noise on every sample, is here a single exact surface, and its peaks are not \
read from a grid but certified algebraically. Take the maximum exactly:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0d268c06-dfaa-4d02-bf65-0f26ec259421"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Maximize", "[", 
  RowBox[{"landscape", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[29]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"fa34a004-2ead-4ef8-8adf-91dac198037e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The maximum returns as a closed-form algebraic number, a root of a cubic \
equal to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["C", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["max",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15e82df2-0f4c-4539-a907-f45e73608f2e"],
 ", with the optimal angles likewise exact ",
 Cell[BoxData["Root"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eb9f1ef7-7718-42ae-ba7f-22c1b8fc1cc7"],
 " expressions. A single QAOA layer does not reach the true cut of ",
 Cell[BoxData["4"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a4719465-05c0-446b-bfd7-6d4b4a4767d3"],
 ", and the exact landscape certifies that ceiling as a cubic root rather \
than an estimate. Falling short is the generic behavior of one layer; a case \
where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03187d86-83ed-4d74-acbe-578616fdca24"],
 " happens to saturate the cut is exceptional, and reaching ",
 Cell[BoxData["4"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38d820af-a3a3-4d41-b8fc-4e38c661980a"],
 " requires deeper QAOA with more layers. The point stands: the variational \
optimum is an exact symbolic quantity, a root of a cubic with closed-form \
angles, not a number sampled near the answer."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bd030cab-dc07-4060-ab5a-873f95e8ebdb"],

Cell["A full many-body computation in closed form", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"3ca7ba6f-a38d-41fa-821d-87950ecb04ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same construction extends to a genuine many-body computation. Build the \
2-qubit Heisenberg Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bd1b403c-684d-4e70-8d89-b8ca3b338d99"],
 " symbolically (Hamiltonian simulation, a central application of a quantum \
computer):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6eedd0b1-d276-4b81-a597-11753c72c6e5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hheis", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"J", " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<XX\>\"", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<YY\>\"", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<ZZ\>\"", "]"}]}], 
    ")"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[30]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"725073e8-cd57-48d6-b75e-c7b21b03e33f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Quench the product state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"01"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d47a935c-1ace-4e1f-ba01-ded5390e55bf"],
 " under it, that is, compute ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], 
    TemplateBox[{"01"},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c2ab2031-a545-4c43-a27b-2e89161022e6"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e122574f-1fca-4ec1-b3ac-a56a24ec2f52"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psit", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{"hheis", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<01\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "t"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[31]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a9e2f64f-949e-4812-a640-7ce01f81867e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Display the evolved state at time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "215a8ab2-2910-4552-820a-0ffb6ba2d4a3"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"45681f66-975d-4a53-a857-a90ba0174afa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "psit", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "TraditionalForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[32]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"df7ef50f-1034-4569-a7f5-2b42d7270267"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The evolved ket displays in closed form: the excitation oscillates \
coherently between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"01"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a0bcc332-fc44-4ddc-a1f1-53478aaca9bb"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"10"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1225e3e0-ddec-4a3e-8a2f-a378117ba7b7"],
 " at angular frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["J", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9a6bca6c-23af-4e08-86d2-be650bfbba1a"],
 ", within an overall phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"i", "J", "t"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "481e5cd7-e202-4670-b9a7-60709edcd790"],
 ". Now read off the entanglement entropy of one qubit as a function of time, \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["log",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "1"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ded61869-8540-4d5f-8dcf-1607db33c957"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "1"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Tr",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e7b5640-6798-4b0c-bd3e-d3c8d4605dbe"],
 ", the standard measure of how entangled the two spins have become and a \
derived, nonlinear quantity:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f98d4285-8623-487d-a023-435c87617900"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
      RowBox[{"psit", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<VonNeumannEntropy\>\"", 
     "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"t", " ", "J"}], " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[33]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"370f3a52-a443-40c7-bbf4-22a61a0ea841"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "QF returns the entire curve as a formula in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12f12b62-5ac9-4305-9887-c1b0786f0680"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["J", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e80d5f32-b632-4943-ba1b-4e4be9769292"],
 ": the binary entropy of the two oscillating populations, zero whenever the \
state is a product, a full bit at the Bell points, periodic with the exchange \
oscillation. Because it is a formula, it can be differentiated, expanded, or \
solved in closed form, and the same approach extends to larger symbolic spin \
chains."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c9c6d517-694e-40ac-ba03-da55606057e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plot it (at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "efb9fd83-126e-44ac-bbc6-d01044c4ddf4"],
 "):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3f0f53f3-41fc-4b7c-8b7a-e6d79282d409"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"s", " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"J", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "Pi"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time  J t\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<entanglement entropy  S(t)  [bits]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[34]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"b37e8639-8c50-43d6-831f-98e2959a4c3f"],

Cell["Claim 2: One object model spans all of quantum theory", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"62a2132a-f987-4b98-bfad-614d64b39332"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Key feature:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Claim 1 developed the symbolic dynamics of one object in depth; this claim \
shows the breadth of the object model. QF provides whole categories of object \
beyond unitary gates: open systems, generalized measurements, \
continuous-variable optics, phase space, and state estimation. Two properties \
hold throughout the model: every object carries its basis, and every object \
is defined in any finite dimension, qutrits and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["N", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57dbe2fe-4d53-4ccd-b55c-37c87800ba87"],
 "-level systems as readily as qubits. The subject here is scope, the range \
of quantum theory that QF represents as objects one computes with directly."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8ef95858-4cc3-4c39-84ee-e540ed2ab725"],

Cell["An open-system object: a quantum channel", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"bdb79bc1-89b7-462d-8224-339b25cbb4bf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A noise process is its own object, a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumChannel"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d77377d0-6136-4180-8584-d028063b80b2"],
 ", not a gate. Take a generic pure qubit on the Bloch sphere, polar angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d1305c84-99cd-4c70-a5f8-1e6de480e7f5"],
 " and azimuth ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9e4f473c-6a71-43f0-a47e-581a365fdeb8"],
 ", and confirm it is pure through the purity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed5b9baf-ff84-4d69-a1b0-2778f78548c6"],
 ", which equals ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33aaf533-6211-4767-badf-79371fdd0a16"],
 " exactly for a pure state and drops below ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d2c51694-7444-4fd5-a4c4-2c30d98cbc60"],
 " for a mixed one. Build the state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9d54ab6f-6a8d-4ad5-b8d2-a3067c37d307"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "/", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[35]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"adb8bb79-e63d-44ea-9ee1-7d4419a46c30"],

Cell["Read its purity:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e0269623-aa93-436d-b771-789d1f71176d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<Purity\>\"", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "FullSimplify"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[36]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7f4a2fb1-9772-4d04-aae4-58c918562a93"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The purity is ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b7a0031-59c6-4621-8420-18d2b46f5aa9"],
 ", as it must be for any pure state."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4c5fcfcd-a7df-4350-86fa-e28c525137f5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Send it through amplitude damping, the decay channel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Function]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "0"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "0", "\[Dagger]"], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "1"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "1", "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f719f6f4-7df4-4e36-aca3-50889a48e906"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "1"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], 
    TemplateBox[{"0"},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{"1"},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dd6afd22-6628-4459-8f60-6f5f920f16b3"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "0"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"], 
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Bra"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{"1", "-", 
       StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], 
     TemplateBox[{"1"},
      "Ket"], 
     TemplateBox[{"1"},
      "Bra"]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c2ec3f0-c687-4540-a545-5a452c1ad68b"],
 ": the excitation is lost with probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7332ee34-c17c-4697-b8c1-1a76cb260512"],
 ", the model of spontaneous emission. The question: how much purity does \
that cost, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalE]", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dd94908f-3c28-45ab-a336-40215c50e51d"],
 ", as an exact function of the damping rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "225663dc-269f-46dd-80f7-39a8c2bdab28"],
 " and the state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bfdc9799-e499-48d5-a40e-b75097bbe279"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<Purity\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QuantumChannel", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<AmplitudeDamping\>\"", "[", "\[Gamma]", "]"}], "]"}], "[",
       "psi", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Purity\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}], 
    "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[37]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7d30c91f-8ec8-4e2b-83a2-22b05572586d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The purity loss returns exactly as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "994161a2-979b-417c-92d3-7071d34a662b"],
 ". The pure input has become mixed: irreversible, non-unitary dynamics \
captured directly as a channel object. The loss depends only on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1968d2d4-8497-4636-8a90-260bb559c309"],
 " and the excited-state weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b16b916a-4f47-4171-9e78-d8d2add170e0"],
 ", never on the azimuth ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dc1f453a-51bb-4be1-885c-460341aeda3e"],
 ", and it vanishes at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eef773cd-8baa-4a42-8f15-78819c2370de"],
 " (no damping), at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2802f35a-f3d8-419f-adef-136a74a768f7"],
 " (fully relaxed to the pure ground state), and at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0650f572-d7d3-4d3b-a07a-49354d24a53f"],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "97d595cc-6d14-4247-acca-f6d14167fa14"],
 ", which damping leaves untouched)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cd6a9d1c-5edd-447d-beb5-fc370038074c"],

Cell["\<\
The master equation, solved once for every state and every rate\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7273c75b-73a2-4e2e-bdf1-c221c8860277"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A channel is a single instance of decoherence; the full dynamics is the \
Lindblad master equation, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "."], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], "{", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "}", 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d0f3e95-89f8-48f7-ae85-02cb9a2488dd"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0fde0086-d9de-406c-b1c9-7eaafbb8201c"],
 " solves it symbolically. Given a density matrix whose four entries are \
symbols and rates that remain symbols, a single solution covers every qubit \
experiment at once. Set the physical region: positive rates, a real level \
splitting, and forward time:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c81a8547-339b-4c8d-aa91-084cc2bbbbec"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$Assumptions", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Gamma]1", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Gamma]\[Phi]", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], " ", "&&", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"t", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[38]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"715382de-7709-4ffb-9b8e-8f334f380eb8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Write the decay operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "-"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"0"},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{"1"},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bdc39a27-a512-4419-b619-c573957cedf0"],
 " as its matrix, so it empties the excited state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2ecd94d6-5813-4da0-b4a0-1c91204e1f4a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[Sigma]m", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[39]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5ec1e466-78d4-496c-803a-e65fc7d3bf36"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Take the all-states-at-once initial density matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0da7465a-4e25-4386-b80f-31c85d6c6026"],
 ", every entry a symbol:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"505ad74f-7d94-4943-b686-9ad53efb4970"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[Rho]0", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[40]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5ccc114d-04a3-41cb-8089-98023b8141af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Solve the master equation for a qubit with level splitting ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8b9f8f0c-f868-429c-9a7f-7706736e9eae"],
 ", energy relaxation at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "799f43fa-8564-45db-ba73-d5d2ab20fa96"],
 " (jump operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "1"]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "-"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f3824df0-07f8-4f76-a33e-d56019ed2466"],
 "), and pure dephasing at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c91d9465-0243-4408-aebd-3fbc4f1b0c8d"],
 " (jump operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]]], " ", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a25a0942-ff8b-483b-a694-6b431a9cf7fe"],
 "):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6f3a30ce-b281-4d69-b9e2-62d24956413b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[Rho]t", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]1", "]"}], " ", "\[Sigma]m"}], ",", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]\[Phi]", "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
    " ", "\[Rho]0", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[41]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"8e4ca648-a33f-4a8d-9922-829a67d55a01"],

Cell["Read its density matrix in the computational basis:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"68651d8a-9d89-4919-b90f-57866ef0f415"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", " ", "/@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]t", "[", "\"\<Computational\>\"", "]"}], 
     "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[42]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"31c49d68-e3f9-4e2e-8874-e8039830968b"],

Cell["\<\
The matrix returns exactly as the complete relaxation law for an arbitrary \
qubit:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"665b4b90-8bf7-4b9a-862c-8f0cfa5978d8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "(", GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], "+", "(", 
       RowBox[{"1", "-", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
         RowBox[{"-", 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "1"], 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}], ")", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "22"]}], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "12"], " ", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"-", "(", 
         RowBox[{
          FractionBox[
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "1"], "2"], "+", "2", 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "+", 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[CapitalOmega]"}], ")", 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]},
     {
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "21"], " ", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"-", "(", 
         RowBox[{
          FractionBox[
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "1"], "2"], "+", "2", 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "-", 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[CapitalOmega]"}], ")", 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "22"], " ", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "1"], 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]}
    }], ")"}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"7796c7cf-202e-4abb-\
a952-6d669747b234"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The excited population decays at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c9999b5-57eb-42ea-8ee1-f266c363692b"],
 ", the lost population moves to the ground state, and the coherence \
precesses at ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fa22d94-5d77-4614-9f35-53cc73c1bfd3"],
 " while decaying at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "1"], "2"], "+", "2", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33e0e819-e9f3-4b9d-b7d3-7979f89eaf31"],
 ": every experiment on every qubit, in one matrix. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"], "=", "1", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "1"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cefe7406-0511-4857-8c04-21936ef5249b"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], "=", "1", "/", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15aa1231-f2ce-43ba-89a4-9f454755690d"],
 " read from the exponents, the textbook bound between the two times is a \
theorem about this solution:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b738a20-52f3-4435-be47-030162f71e71"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Reduce", "[", 
  RowBox[{"ForAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]1", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]\[Phi]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]1", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]\[Phi]", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"1", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Gamma]1", "/", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]\[Phi]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "<=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", "/", "\[Gamma]1"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[43]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6d9c37c1-3bdf-467c-bb73-f3d8a6da8da6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The reduction returns ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e161ada-2815-470e-a539-719a1394dbf2"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], "\[LessEqual]", "2", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "764ba6ab-4d6a-4a58-a5bf-27163e44cf5e"],
 " holds for every admissible rate pair, obtained from the computation rather \
than quoted from a textbook, and reducing the corresponding equality for the \
dephasing rate, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Reduce", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"1", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Gamma]1", "/", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]\[Phi]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", "/", "\[Gamma]1"}]}], ",", " ", "\[Gamma]\[Phi]"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "94db3239-fc5f-4eb3-80a1-b5bdafcaf820"],
 ", returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f01f75da-25f7-4a5f-a510-f4eee09e8ba8"],
 " (for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "1"], "\[NotEqual]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c6c4988a-154d-4ab8-80d2-d0963d93d6c4"],
 "): the factor of two is saturated exactly when dephasing vanishes."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3783b34e-f936-4e8c-8e73-56470f96da5a"],

Cell["A generalized measurement: a POVM", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7f3cc338-a80a-4765-aa72-7191a4c51bc5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Real detectors are not always projective. A POVM is a set of positive \
effects ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8f0d9bed-1d72-451f-83a1-18a98544dc0e"],
 " summing to the identity, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "91dc8804-c881-43a7-85df-592e44ef7050"],
 ", with outcome probabilities given by the Born rule ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a0c271a-2fef-4657-b330-94e769519eb3"],
 "; one is built from a list of effects with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"E1", ",", " ", "E2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e857873-f0e8-4e5b-8735-87251fe1b20c"],
 ". A ",
 StyleBox["symmetric informationally complete", "TI"],
 " POVM is the maximally symmetric case: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b21e054-a89e-4db3-912c-f2f9c1c16a25"],
 " rank-one effects ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
    TemplateBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]]},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]]},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c1061bc2-541a-49b7-bbfe-a91a57985f32"],
 " with equal pairwise overlaps ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       TemplateBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]]},
        "BraKet"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67d48d9b-3d1c-4dec-8f5f-0b9c3980b36f"],
 ", four outcomes on a two-level system, pointing along the vertices of a \
tetrahedron in the Bloch ball. Measure a generic Bloch qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5a7acf66-301d-4f80-905e-550d3a24fe5b"],
 ", applying the Born rule symbolically to all four effects. Build the \
state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e800b6c3-40a4-420e-b428-7d6b8d9c621b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "/", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[44]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"fa197021-b603-4a80-ad73-e5f88ddad2cb"],

Cell["Build the tetrahedron SIC POVM:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f987244a-e9a3-4b6d-9ccc-ad0c69531131"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"sic", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
  "QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", "\"\<TetrahedronSICPOVM\>\"", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[45]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e863e46c-0806-4d4f-a276-02dcdb8fa640"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Apply the Born rule ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b0fd20a7-b972-4293-8c53-3c5088a973ae"],
 " to all four effects at once:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eedaa30d-05ce-41c7-a4c2-7d4d956e1ef1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"probs", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Normal", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"sic", "[", "\"\<POVMElements\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[46]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a49d6f22-7f5d-44f8-a97b-6f1721ac4d6d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The four probabilities return exactly as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "4"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], "1", "+", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "^"], "\[CenterDot]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fedb573-8f30-47aa-a8a6-b5d6218fea24"],
 ", the first reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox[
   RowBox[{"1", "+", 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}], "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6624dbcd-6f73-4c56-b425-319a6bbc2824"],
 " and the others ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "12"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], "3", "-", 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "+", 
   SqrtBox["2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Ellipsis]", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8dc6aa20-4b36-47e1-9619-ed467bb7ab4f"],
 " along the remaining tetrahedron directions ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fc9383a8-fa27-4a93-bf61-3da9c45e5ca1"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "86279d70-419f-4622-9fbf-d33c4f950e23"],
 " the state's Bloch vector; they sum to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ca8ec24-db6f-4a3e-947f-cb79589f5167"],
 " identically (verified). Pin the state to the north pole and the general \
formulas collapse to numbers:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cd95d0f4-1d4c-4c69-a09a-f481a08a9a09"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"probs", " ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[47]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"92dd8dbd-2c93-4974-b796-6b53a1593ef2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The distribution collapses to simple rationals: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e952f421-7b24-4314-bab8-6ffb1a378da6"],
 " assigns probability one half to the tetrahedron vertex nearest the pole \
and one sixth to each of the other three. Because the SIC is informationally \
complete, these four probabilities are not merely statistics of the state; \
they determine the state: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05a52f5b-d6ba-4314-afaf-86299b6cdc5a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "789c63d0-8082-4cd3-897d-713684be6259"],
 " can be recovered from them, which is what makes SIC measurements a natural \
basis for tomography."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66effe7c-2a02-4512-8d29-67d04429952c"],

Cell["\<\
The SIC is not only a symbolic Born-rule calculation; it is a measurement \
that drops directly into a circuit, alongside the gates, on any chosen wire. \
Place the tetrahedron SIC as a measurement on the first qubit:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8ff87cf0-ada1-43c6-8e4e-e38b5ce5329a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"sicQubit1", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<TetrahedronSICPOVM\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[48]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7f2875bc-2467-4b08-95a3-bbdf22dd8f33"],

Cell["Build a small entangling circuit that ends in that POVM:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7cc3ca1e-8ec9-4059-84cf-f4eaed7c9007"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"circ", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<RY\>\"", "[", "1.05", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", 
     "\n", "       ", "\"\<CNOT\>\"", " ", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<RZ\>\"", "[", "2.04", "]"}], ",", " ", "sicQubit1"}], "}"}],
    "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[49]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"9bb47dd7-b885-4ad1-a46f-95f0ca426fd7"],

Cell["Draw it:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bdd0d1fd-c94f-4100-8953-badfa81c9fb7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"circ", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[50]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"43a04621-ff22-4a41-849d-f8dcb73c10d8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The diagram shows the four-outcome POVM sitting at the end of the first \
wire like any other measurement. Applying the circuit returns a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a563485-788d-41b4-90ff-e20bb96f7c49"],
 ", and that object draws its own outcome statistics:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f694cc17-fe04-41f8-9b9b-91f77974c835"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"circ", "[", "]"}], "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesPlot\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[51]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"38171e3a-f297-48e4-a470-8e4c733b7813"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Four bars summing to one, one tetrahedron outcome suppressed and another \
enhanced: the SIC measurement of qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d1751cf-4f0e-4980-842e-da2082133302"],
 ". Here qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a5fb0d04-1d98-44ad-910b-20a6b0293f91"],
 " is entangled with qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3068251a-8e29-42cd-be77-500a687dca88"],
 ", so its reduced state is mixed, its Bloch vector lies inside the ball \
(length less than ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bb08586-a620-49f4-a3a0-42916dcbebae"],
 "), and the four probabilities are correspondingly drawn in from the \
pure-state extremes toward the uniform value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7afd7bfa-97af-4262-b7c5-ef3a8effa675"],
 ". The same informationally complete measurement reports a mixed, entangled \
qubit as faithfully as a pure one, which is what tomography of a real, noisy \
qubit requires."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6c583720-1986-4459-b909-b9e11b8112bb"],

Cell["Continuous-variable quantum optics", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"fc85c76a-6b40-478c-85f4-5effeba7a6c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Bosonic Fock space, not qubits. The state of an ideal laser mode is the \
coherent state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
         {
          StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
        },
        GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
        GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", "2"}]], 
    RowBox[{
     UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "0"}], "\[Infinity]",
      LimitsPositioning->False], 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
       SqrtBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}]]], 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
       "Ket"]}]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39120511-0804-485b-ace4-0c879a0f6c4f"],
 ", defined as the eigenstate of the photon annihilation operator, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b69ede5-0c42-46da-b3b4-dbec915dd8c0"],
 ", with a complex eigenvalue ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d1a80e2-9e7b-4e3c-9d3c-b1355c699a8a"],
 " because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fb1dbba-f02c-47e1-9e9d-5e6932571a25"],
 " is not Hermitian. QF builds these objects directly in a truncated Fock \
space (sixteen levels by default). Check the eigenvalue equation with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9892bc09-63a7-417d-808a-b61ae18e6708"],
 " fully symbolic. Build the annihilation operator:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"475e0940-97a2-497c-b927-932da0a1310f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"aOp", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[52]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"704e16a8-1fbb-4c99-9954-a8f065907ee4"],

Cell["\<\
Build the coherent state, left unnormalized so the symbolic algebra stays \
clean:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5a1036c7-40d0-4849-b7cc-4cd98f8508ca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"alphaKet", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"CoherentState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Normalized\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[53]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"df2db0f0-0fd4-453e-b0f6-be611a7a6255"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Subtract ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "018e3ca3-9778-4efa-a545-fa2441e5a436"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a165cd3b-f287-49a6-96a3-6917afe170e5"],
 " and read the amplitudes (the truncation edge excluded):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"921ef5a2-81fc-41c9-bd1e-ac06b0f016b3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Most", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"aOp", "[", "alphaKet", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[FormalAlpha]", " ", "alphaKet"}]}], ")"}], 
    "[", "\"\<AmplitudesList\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[54]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c12ecdb5-7a7c-4ed4-825a-9cacc58d8784"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every amplitude of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "-", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e0beeed4-0185-4e58-9115-b85e8d12270e"],
 " returns identically zero in the symbolic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fddc95c-e186-4a3f-9ff2-6351b6ac9d26"],
 " (the truncation-edge amplitude excluded): the defining equation, verified \
for the whole family of coherent states at once."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"acd23c40-25cc-49d6-8e71-e136be241211"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The property that earns these states the name \"most classical states of \
light\" is dynamical: under the oscillator Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d583af14-7bb2-4042-9f5a-d336343ae3a9"],
 " a coherent state remains a coherent state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], 
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
         RowBox[{"-", 
           StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1fb2a869-eac2-4407-81b0-d4ab9a733602"],
 ", its label ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d31a42bb-c151-4555-a853-d4f8f40ef2b2"],
 " rotating about the origin of phase space at frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d6fb7c23-6fc9-4ae8-ab34-76acb17780b0"],
 ", like a classical oscillator amplitude, up to the overall phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "760fef4a-2f8d-4a2e-bc2f-4c7e8ae4911b"],
 ". Compute the oscillator propagator with ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e729283-a689-4716-bc33-209d2c4dc044"],
 ", symbolically:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b2ea1ae0-2c8d-46ab-a887-ff69531cc8c6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"uosc", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"aOp", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", "aOp"}], 
       " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "None", ",", " ", "t"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[55]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7268cdf2-6058-4f71-a869-50cbd9253c58"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Then check the coherent-state identity it implies, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "919a42ab-402f-4803-bab5-d1d2e64568fa"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36653979-7139-4334-87d7-88c20fefa8d8"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e7e515b-d8a9-48aa-b7f1-5f05dbb83d0b"],
 " all symbols:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"052a3c33-a251-4e02-a8d3-d54f294bbb9e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"uosc", " ", "@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"CoherentState", "[", "]"}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"E", "^", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "\[Omega]", " ", 
      RowBox[{"t", "/", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"CoherentState", "[", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[FormalAlpha]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"E", "^", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "\[Omega]", " ", "t"}], ")"}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[56]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6d143de5-cd43-4841-8d4f-d6caf3809f9c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d6ef3f90-7081-4b9f-9ed9-2567eff04521"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d0e069be-7d53-4975-ae89-9017c6f80d47"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d33836c5-e749-4a28-b738-686a77a50684"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bec31092-5dae-45a8-b34f-19f053d981fe"],
 " all symbols: one evolution determines the dynamics of every coherent state \
at every frequency, an exact statement about the family rather than a \
simulation of one member. (QF's state ",
 Cell[BoxData["=="], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e109678c-49b1-4c67-a3ce-23e6a4bb6ee6"],
 " compares up to global phase, so this fixes the label ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", 
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "567fa28a-28de-4556-b81a-fb569fc33598"],
 "; the vacuum phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bb0a78c9-1cda-4299-9818-625cf52df8d2"],
 " is exact but lies in the global phase that ",
 Cell[BoxData["=="], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6476243d-5498-4bdc-92a7-0d4b851c7375"],
 " ignores, and appears only in an amplitude-level comparison.)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4610bda1-5bc7-475d-ba8b-2ce54621ba7c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "What distinguishes this most-classical light from other states is photon \
statistics. The second-order coherence at zero delay, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "2", 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], " ", 
      StyleBox["a", "TI"]}], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
       StyleBox["a", "TI"]}], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f2800f3-d46c-4644-a71a-c045b2974d2f"],
 ", is the normalized probability of detecting two photons at once; it \
classifies light by photon statistics: antibunched (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "140ea862-ffd9-4e25-be3c-50e4ccdde673"],
 ", nonclassical), coherent (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bb4832d5-8679-45f7-9cc0-25cedb1fa4ba"],
 "), and bunched thermal (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{">", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09e3013a-1b2d-46d5-b60c-474f0c9fdcff"],
 ")."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0b40ee4c-8b29-49a2-9190-05b668cb3379"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"g2s", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"<|", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\"\<Fock\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"G2Coherence", "[", 
      RowBox[{"FockState", "[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"G2Coherence", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"CoherentState", "[", "20", "]"}], "[", "1.5", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
    ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Thermal\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"G2Coherence", "[", 
      RowBox[{"ThermalState", "[", 
       RowBox[{"1.0", ",", " ", "20"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[57]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"14f43036-60e4-4c03-a1a7-75a0c5a67887"],

Cell["\<\
Each class takes the value the formula predicts: zero for the single photon, \
one for the laser, two for thermal light. The three values chart directly:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bf917e57-a55a-4944-9dda-34e758107958"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"BarChart", "[", 
  RowBox[{"g2s", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ChartLabels", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Fock |1\[RightAngleBracket]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<Coherent\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Thermal\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Second-order coherence g2(0)\>\""}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "2.2"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[58]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2e9b0761-d8a1-4c3d-9b74-92c3f7b96c25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ordering on the chart, antibunched below ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b04a99db-6d96-4783-9634-6c54b70cd82a"],
 ", coherent at ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fd0b7248-5c62-45f5-993a-9bfebb045a5b"],
 ", bunched above, is the photon-statistics signature that distinguishes \
these light sources where a single intensity measurement cannot."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"af1ce34b-819a-4efc-a584-dc24befd85f7"],

Cell["Phase-space quasi-probabilities: Wigner and Husimi", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"52af68f3-63df-4d4f-bfeb-f911fa6a3dea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Wigner function is the phase-space quasi-probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "\[Pi]"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Integral]",
      FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
          StyleBox["y", "TI"]}]},
       "Bra"], 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      TemplateBox[{
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "+", 
          StyleBox["y", "TI"]}]},
       "Ket"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{"2", 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["y", "TI"]}]], 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["y", "TI"]}]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b677fd69-bd02-4afe-a19e-2c04fd44edcf"],
 ". It integrates to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cc73d0b-a87b-4c94-909b-cfe8e49d6671"],
 " like a probability density but, unlike one, can take negative values, and \
that negativity is a signature of nonclassicality with no classical analogue. \
A clear example is the Schrodinger cat state, the even superposition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     TemplateBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
         StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", "\|01d4a9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ddbf5f3-4cb6-4755-aa00-2cd032ba82fe"],
 " of two coherent states of opposite phase, here with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a794c59-fb6a-4c57-b347-ebbef066d80d"],
 ". Build its Wigner function on a phase-space window:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a15cfba2-81a6-49f6-9b6f-4d3def2b7ed9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"wigner", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"WignerRepresentation", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"CatState", "[", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "2"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<GridSize\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "90"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[59]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c20a2ac7-876c-4e32-94a1-1eab5befb11e"],

Cell["\<\
Read it at two representative points, the origin and half a fringe away in \
momentum:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fc42a81d-6a9d-4f5f-afd6-c62a77c52d2e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"wigner", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"wigner", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[60]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a2f2cc33-5d10-434e-8a5f-cf0da610d1f7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first value is positive, the second negative. The first is the \
important one: at the midpoint between the two coherent components, where a \
classical mixture of them would place almost no weight, the Wigner function \
instead has its strongest feature, an interference peak that reaches the \
ceiling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ca40a6dd-f4bb-4ee5-98a1-ef2ef45538c2"],
 " that no Wigner function can exceed. The even cat is a parity eigenstate, \
so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "1", "/", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79dc9c11-3587-4213-8552-4bf0c42667f7"],
 " exactly (here up to the Fock truncation), not merely close to it; the \
neighboring fringe is firmly negative."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"adb0230c-0186-4219-98fc-02060f3cb45c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Wigner function is one of a family of phase-space quasi-probabilities, \
and its smoothed counterpart removes the negativity. The Husimi-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3dafdb68-df60-4932-8f09-450f4fc4e2e2"],
 " function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "\[Pi]"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
     "Bra"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "766d8983-cc72-4745-b4a8-2a4e351b1383"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56b963f1-9523-4a32-9397-77138eca9f3b"],
 ", is the Wigner function convolved with a coherent-state Gaussian; that \
smoothing makes it non-negative everywhere, at the cost of removing the \
nonclassicality the Wigner reveals. Build it over the same window, slightly \
taller in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "feabe78a-4868-4eab-8348-cb854dfd9818"],
 " since the Husimi is wider:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fd52b80b-d5c5-46d7-9425-fee9e32e0be1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"husimi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"HusimiQRepresentation", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"CatState", "[", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<GridSize\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "90"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[61]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ed477078-e4d6-418c-b0c1-c04aa77b4c61"],

Cell["Read it at the origin where the Wigner peaked:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"577e6d07-fa63-41d5-8e92-468809889014"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"husimi", "[", 
  RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[62]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"89bb5250-40cb-495a-820a-e774d0c56d26"],

Cell["\<\
The Husimi is close to zero there, in contrast to the Wigner's sharp peak: \
the Gaussian average has cancelled the oscillating fringes. Plot the two \
surfaces side by side:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"99a219c3-7a55-43ae-899f-bd94f0596b50"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Plot3D", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"wigner", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "2"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Mesh", " ", "->", " ", "None"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotPoints", " ", "->", " ", "50"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<SunsetColors\>\""}], ",", 
      "\n", "     ", 
      RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<p\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<W\>\""}], 
        "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Wigner W(x,p)\>\""}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "Small"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
    "   ", 
    RowBox[{"Plot3D", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"husimi", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Mesh", " ", "->", " ", "None"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotPoints", " ", "->", " ", "50"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<SunsetColors\>\""}], ",", 
      "\n", "     ", 
      RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<p\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Q\>\""}], 
        "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Husimi Q(x,p)\>\""}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "Small"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[63]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"28d709e7-b607-43b1-b94f-1e20ea20b28f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same cat state, two quasi-probabilities. The Wigner on the left has the \
two Gaussian lobes at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", "2", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "706b805d-4c79-4148-9734-91ed237a463d"],
 ", the coherent components, together with the interference ridge oscillating \
above and below zero between them; that negativity is the signature of the \
superposition. The Husimi on the right keeps only the two smooth, \
non-negative lobes, each near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "2", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8258292f-68d2-4401-b7f2-932ae64b8f1d"],
 ", with the fringes smoothed flat. Both are properly normalized \
quasi-probabilities, the Wigner integrating to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06f19a69-14b3-4ac7-83e8-2132eeb49917"],
 " over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e2f050f-0083-4e99-aefa-e132df1b5ceb"],
 " and the Husimi to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e5fa179-b112-48f3-a1b1-6bcdbc5bfe40"],
 " over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8f65d467-beca-435a-b956-ee40d06325e8"],
 " (equivalently, to ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f38aaaf-a4a2-4db6-bb1e-7dcfe13d44a7"],
 " over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d365c6f5-deef-4c02-a877-cf0a33c80af7"],
 "), but only the Wigner can take negative values, which is why Wigner \
negativity, and not the always-positive Husimi, is the witness of \
nonclassicality. Decoherence erases the Wigner fringes and leaves the lobes, \
moving the left picture toward the right."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1281aa35-c48f-4019-9841-789de75c45ac"],

Cell["Every object carries its basis", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"c5a096bc-a6fd-46da-9728-97e8c20e8429"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The scope extends inward as well: every state, operator, and measurement \
above is stored together with the basis it is written in. A basis is a stored \
matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2bca0e59-744a-436a-b503-18e942854b10"],
 " whose rows are the basis vectors in computational coordinates, a change of \
basis is the similarity transformation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[ScriptCapitalB]"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["B", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a219c94-6e09-4f21-9a00-325adfda21b2"],
 ", and objects written in different bases reconcile automatically through \
the computational frame. About three dozen named bases are provided (Bell, \
Fourier, Schwinger, Dirac, Gell-Mann, Wigner, MUB, SIC), and the same \
mechanism converts non-computational measurements for OpenQASM export and \
supplies the Bell-derived basis used in two-qubit KAK gate compilation. The \
representation changes while the physics does not: take the qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70a74d59-f708-4035-bd9d-ce8e72ddb3a6"],
 ", the superposition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     TemplateBox[{"1"},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c56391c1-aafc-4ab6-b176-ca93adf667fc"],
 " in the computational basis, and write it in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ddeaa52-fec4-49fc-9924-5782d350c595"],
 " basis instead:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"826c29df-4071-4fb9-a341-185984a9b203"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<+\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<X\>\""}], 
   "]"}], " ", "//", " ", "TraditionalForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[64]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e8b21550-8713-4af4-be87-f36c2c754623"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The state renders as the single ket ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "+"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3191c68a-992f-4d9c-aae8-4e1c84224d87"],
 ": in its own eigenbasis ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cf64d775-2262-4b90-ab42-e5e7b650d4d0"],
 " is one basis vector, not a superposition. Same state, different \
coordinates."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"21ad7720-f04d-419d-b4f0-812f635bfb70"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The measurable content is untouched by any such rewriting, and nothing here \
is qubit-bound. Take a spin-1 particle in its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d52797c-86c6-429f-b544-c1dc02f74d1c"],
 " eigenstate, defined directly in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "705d00af-d08a-4695-9ed6-e97f5672ad28"],
 " basis:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e433429c-0a58-4534-bb6f-c199bd2915dc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mx", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<JX\>\"", "[", "1", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[65]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c2e9c9c0-ccda-47c0-ba31-ef22ecbdf117"],

Cell["Display it:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"18ce0123-5693-4ccd-9d2f-16a357dc0be0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mx", " ", "//", " ", "TraditionalForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[66]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"9c1c57e4-790b-4694-8762-db2d949d6e2b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The state renders as the single ket ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["J", "TI"], "1", 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fabbf3d-2efd-4b42-9e96-0e3abe9b273f"],
 ". Re-express it in the computational (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8d21bebd-931f-4396-80b0-74a6e98812bb"],
 ") basis:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0156ede0-1541-4fad-962b-7a84949fa891"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mxZ", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"mx", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Computational\>\"", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[67]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e9ba3947-1d5b-4261-a69f-90992f2aae94"],

Cell["Display it again:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d0848157-aae6-473b-a0d2-d913bf60eb7c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mxZ", " ", "//", " ", "TraditionalForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[68]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"f8691803-c4a1-49f0-8e8b-6033c835024d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same state spreads into a three-term superposition over the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f1bca6f-cdb1-412a-9aca-8d04b08397fd"],
 " levels: one ket in its own basis, a sum in the other. The named operator \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4495d4dd-5a28-4b1a-a664-511ea56140a2"],
 " is itself stored in its own eigenbasis, so the expectation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Bra"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e5ddca6f-1919-46e5-a416-b4c6a651f753"],
 " involves three declared bases at once; compute it from both \
representations of the state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8340d7ab-721e-4a76-8af0-ceaab1818b15"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<JX basis\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"mx", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<JX\>\"", "[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "mx", "]"}], "]"}],
      "[", "\"\<Scalar\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Computational basis\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"mxZ", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<JX\>\"", "[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "mxZ", "]"}], 
      "]"}], "[", "\"\<Scalar\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[69]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2830ac5b-651d-4709-b6ea-85ff13d1a8db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both entries return as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ee2c0490-078f-4cec-ad3f-8ddb08701bd0"],
 ": the state in either coordinate system, the operator in a third, and QF \
reconciled them all; the invariant survives every change of coordinates."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c9359328-b577-41e1-ab25-ab2f8ee9664f"],

Cell["Any finite dimension: a spin-1 qutrit and a five-site ring", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d8338626-0fd7-452f-acee-725103025d4d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same spin-1 system supports genuine three-level dynamics, not just a \
change of basis, and the representation extends to any dimension. Its \
zero-field-splitting Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], " ", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["y", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9104cbd3-a174-40da-9d66-4aca441d9c4d"],
 ", the model of an NV-center defect, is built from QF's native spin-1 \
operators with both couplings left symbolic. First the three spin-1 operators:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d582b1de-abea-4e5c-91de-0aae7e7ec099"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"jx", ",", " ", "jy", ",", " ", "jz"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", " ", "/@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<JX\>\"", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<JY\>\"", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<JZ\>\"", "[", "1", "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[70]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a846939e-5473-43c7-9a91-63a7678f0ddc"],

Cell["Assemble the zero-field-splitting Hamiltonian from them:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3bdffd38-4fda-4927-b453-7c72d9e6a4c3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hzfs", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[FormalD]", " ", 
    RowBox[{"jz", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[FormalE]", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"jx", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"jy", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[71]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c40d23b3-13c9-4cce-ba38-71d6ddb69cb5"],

Cell["Display its matrix:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8379a21a-9de9-4912-a2ca-2f1af9719cab"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hzfs", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[72]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"41727c3f-df43-4416-b1d9-e347a0f00d5a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The operator is fully symbolic, and its matrix is displayed in the basis \
the algebra carried with it, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed578245-54d6-4e13-b296-ab8631527f2a"],
 " eigenbasis: the couplings remain symbols, and the coordinates remain \
attached to the object."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dd71caec-f3de-4f08-bdcc-ed1189bdd96e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A Hamiltonian is simplest in its energy eigenbasis, and the operator \
provides its own eigenvectors. Build a basis from them and read ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8be97a00-4a8a-483a-85c8-37a44990de9b"],
 " there:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"80577566-b352-4b21-b5b7-8a88cd3410d2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
     RowBox[{"hzfs", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"QuantumBasis", "[", 
       RowBox[{"hzfs", "[", "\"\<Eigenvectors\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", "Normal"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "FullSimplify"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[73]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4086cae2-83d8-4ff6-a059-7a0a21f995b9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The matrix returns exactly as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["diag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited], "0"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"]}], "-", 
     StyleBox["e", "TI"]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"]}], "+", 
     StyleBox["e", "TI"]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "619f860c-050a-4200-ab93-c7b587ee0dde"],
 ": the zero-field-split spectrum in closed form, symbols intact. Building a \
basis from an object's own eigenvectors works in any dimension, and the spin-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9b2813c0-4eb9-4819-943a-b01d0f2764b9"],
 " operators are provided natively for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f2e50e53-0b79-479c-93f7-49aa095777f8"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c4845fb5-4826-4892-b5dd-0c902621026f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Dimension need not be a power of two either. A particle hopping on an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["N", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cadd7d2-af96-4d9a-92fe-fd3821d02d30"],
 "-site ring lives in an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["N", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ca0066dc-293a-495d-b8cf-8a1502034aea"],
 "-dimensional Hilbert space, here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], "=", "5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ebf251d4-93b4-458b-b7bc-8553b6339dc6"],
 ", with the tight-binding Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    RowBox[{
     UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["j", "TI"], "=", "1"}], 
      StyleBox["N", "TI"],
      LimitsPositioning->False], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        TemplateBox[{
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]},
         "Ket"], 
        TemplateBox[{
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["j", "TI"], "+", "1"}]},
         "Bra"]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        TemplateBox[{
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["j", "TI"], "+", "1"}]},
         "Ket"], 
        TemplateBox[{
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]},
         "Bra"]}]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "476a3d97-6276-4659-a1a3-5a0d092f2d52"],
 ", site ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7056eea4-a843-4112-b70a-0e7527ef201a"],
 " identified with site ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6df80749-2941-485e-97d3-d8b24f61de88"],
 ". Fix the ring size:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d40e5bed-f1e3-4556-926f-b32fd102d07a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", "5"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[74]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c65db64b-4712-4f46-8916-af66e2c80012"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build the hopping matrix, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0600c37c-0a79-4814-af80-633d57d5c06d"],
 " for every pair of neighboring sites:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"522ddda6-c2b0-4159-ada8-c6d3528567c9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ring", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Boole", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Mod", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"i", " ", "-", " ", "j"}], ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], " ", "==",
          " ", "1"}], " ", "||", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Mod", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"j", " ", "-", " ", "i"}], ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], " ", "==",
          " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[75]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"06225525-05f7-4558-89ad-179bc18370e5"],

Cell["Look at it in the site basis:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7beff456-9f68-4fe7-8603-0f074b43adc8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ring", " ", "//", " ", "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[76]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ba58ed04-3cb1-4363-b571-b31fe0aa9007"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The matrix displays as a circulant: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f06c4bcd-ad4b-4631-bee5-aa3857c7c241"],
 " on the two neighbor diagonals and in the far corners, the bond that closes \
the chain into a ring, and zero everywhere else. In the site basis the \
physics is local hopping; by Bloch's theorem the same operator should be \
diagonal in the momentum (Fourier) basis. Rewrite it there and read the \
diagonal:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aad22f9a-2e53-4c04-bbee-749fd482a4e3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Normal", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Chop", " ", "@", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"N", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Diagonal", "[", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "ring", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"QuantumBasis", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Fourier\>\"", "[", "n", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
      "\n", "     ", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[77]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6890c6af-fe4f-48f9-b31a-55059a4deb5b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The diagonal returns exactly the tight-binding dispersion ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "-", "2", 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "/", 
    StyleBox["N", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bea6b60e-76c9-4006-b6b4-ce61e5a150f5"],
 " at the five Bloch momenta, and the off-diagonal terms vanish: a five-level \
system, diagonalized by a named basis the same way a qubit would be."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a595bda0-5839-40e5-bf08-de80a9ab100a"],

Cell["State estimation: tomography from measured counts", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"eac8783e-45d7-4d7f-8cc3-fa3c9fac6318"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Tomography is the inverse of measurement: recover an unknown state from the \
statistics of measurements in several bases, and it is part of the same \
object model. The three qubit Pauli bases ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e40f6e27-e9fa-45ef-a82e-9af2939992de"],
 " are mutually unbiased and together informationally complete: their outcome \
frequencies estimate the three expectations that pin down the density matrix \
through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10038508-f340-495c-b824-1f97c7aa4d73"],
 ". QF performs the entire procedure. First, pick an unknown state to \
reconstruct:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"95e1534d-6fde-42fe-a0d5-89b998e2d0d9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"true", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"N", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "6"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "6"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
        RowBox[{"I", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[78]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"71c09975-a0e7-4717-990c-75494f487bea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Simulate ",
 Cell[BoxData["2000"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e06367d5-a00f-46e1-88da-3d3e85e4a8cd"],
 " measurement shots in each of the three Pauli bases (seeded for \
reproducibility):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"53bf30c6-e696-47ed-9c9e-bc54f6c40139"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "42", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"data", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementSimulation", "[", 
    RowBox[{"true", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementOperator", " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Y\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Z\>\""}], 
       "}"}]}], ",", " ", "2000"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[79]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7e22390d-6137-43c1-ac93-5812b365b246"],

Cell["Look at the raw counts:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"30f1fa15-d9e3-46ee-9060-dfc7153e67f9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Values", "[", "data", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[80]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a492e2f7-4b2b-42e6-9ed5-1e4661149276"],

Cell["\<\
Three pairs of counts return, one per basis: multinomially sampled tallies \
scattered around the Born-rule proportions, different on every fresh sample, \
and all a real experiment ever sees.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b12a616e-f7fd-42b1-84d3-aff2bb632f62"],

Cell["\<\
Now pass the counts to the estimator, which performs linear inversion \
followed by maximum-likelihood:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9977af8d-fb99-4f7d-870f-421564f20e58"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"est", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumStateEstimate", "[", "data", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[81]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"8ce1902a-a09e-4c92-af3c-23b3fd63004f"],

Cell["Read the reconstructed density matrix:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fa7c3074-b76e-403e-b1c8-03306efcfd48"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"est", "[", "\"\<MaximumLikelihoodState\>\"", "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", "Normal"}], " ", "//",
   " ", "Chop"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[82]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e9a7db40-c6eb-4297-933b-dd4f0fdc9c3f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The recovered matrix agrees closely with the true one, whose exact entries \
are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "11"], "=", 
   FractionBox["3", "4"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6603ae3b-a486-46d0-b3b4-8925884cc67f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "12"], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SqrtBox["3"], "4"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f0bacef2-3126-4dd4-9b1a-0b95efd99673"],
 ", with entry-wise residuals at the scale shot noise sets, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Tilde]", "1", "/", 
   SqrtBox["2000"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0bf56ca3-dab8-4c49-af19-a4cf46a9160c"],
 "; which entries deviate, and by how much, changes with every fresh sample. \
To summarize the reconstruction in one number, compute its fidelity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SqrtBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], " ", 
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], " ", 
     SqrtBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bb99d9a5-cb55-4218-a647-e2271652a1d7"],
 " to the original state, equal to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25aaa931-d972-436a-85c2-6048d180f7ec"],
 " exactly when the two states coincide:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7cfc8322-3bcd-48f0-9b92-11c11916819a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"QuantumSimilarity", "[", 
  RowBox[{"true", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"est", "[", "\"\<MaximumLikelihoodState\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[83]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6ffd360e-08cf-435f-b9b5-c3db79e7d4e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The fidelity is close to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1744f196-c26b-4423-8be2-be2e2d78394c"],
 ", its deviation set by the shot noise, of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox["2000"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62fa10d7-2376-4b5d-a54d-b0ec1800891c"],
 ": the unknown state recovered from finite, noisy synthetic data, using only \
counts in three bases. Beyond these unitary measurement bases, the same basis \
mechanism continues into the over-complete operator frames, where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "844157e2-d291-4f75-b7a3-f101e022f875"],
 " becomes a dual frame and a state becomes a probability vector, the \
mechanism behind the SIC measurement above."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"82bd3ab3-b8a5-4b88-8229-923a1741316c"],

Cell["\<\
Claim 3: Measurement records are quantum wires, and feedforward is a \
controlled gate\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7a14127e-7eaa-4906-b481-69c85889ab75"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Key feature:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Claim 2 used measurement to estimate a state; here measurement itself is \
decomposed. QF implements a projective measurement as von Neumann's \
measurement interaction, not as a collapse: it appends a pointer qudit and \
entangles it with the system, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
       TemplateBox[{
         StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
        "Ket"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], "\[CircleTimes]", 
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
      "Ket"]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "694e67e8-068b-423b-b54a-c74fbfa18f89"],
 ". The record of the measurement is therefore itself a quantum wire, \
numbered ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "2"}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51238556-cf76-4a48-8537-c29bfd107552"],
 " alongside the system wires; every branch remains in the state, and \
feedforward, acting on the system conditioned on an earlier outcome, is \
simply a gate controlled on a record wire. Protocols that combine measurement \
with conditioned gates, teleportation, error correction, measurement-based \
computing, remain inside one symbolic object."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dad9d941-8c19-4724-8def-a4858dd6a7f2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Closest competitor.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Cirq and PennyLane both ship a ",
 Cell[BoxData["defer_measurements"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d35550a-9c46-400d-a293-d1275973abd7"],
 " transform that turns mid-circuit measurement into exactly this \
controlled-on-a-record mechanism; QF's edge is generality, not kind: \
arbitrary observables, degenerate rank-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "245d595a-5684-4886-af84-d923f465dd9f"],
 " projectors, POVM and Naimark dilations, qudits, and a record that can be \
read jointly and inverted, not just a deferred computational-basis bit."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1c944f7d-b721-4bb0-a418-0a8f5a88bb94"],

Cell["Teleportation: the classical channel as a quantum wire", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"88383d8e-c1f2-4e29-aa1d-60ac5d9fb3e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Teleportation is the clearest illustration of a measurement record used as \
a wire. In the textbook protocol Alice measures her two qubits in the Bell \
basis and sends the two classical bits to Bob, who applies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], "1"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "93ff0908-95af-417e-89fe-85cadd54a8b0"],
 " to his half of an entangled pair. The deferred-measurement principle \
states that this classical communication is not required: the corrections can \
be conditioned on the records themselves. Build exactly that, qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e5623642-348b-487c-ac05-e1a1a0f46455"],
 " carrying the unknown state, qubits ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06d540f1-a303-4bd4-84f2-89a8e5be392d"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["3"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b0b4ae4-8b30-44f7-bf91-b5c4ffbba153"],
 " in a Bell pair:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"db388228-518d-4925-9356-6cf4e1cace07"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tele", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[84]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3a4ed963-dfff-407d-85ef-9d1f2e74f648"],

Cell["Draw the protocol:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dccee730-591f-4292-a218-a77f43eeb68b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tele", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[85]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"da1932bc-06f3-4319-a671-8358ad66825b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The diagram is the whole protocol. The two measurements, written as the \
bare qubit lists ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e6175e27-569b-4ec2-b8be-607671cac3cd"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e5897a60-367c-4758-937c-4e6d9c38fc6c"],
 ", place their outcomes on the record wires described in the introduction, \
numbered ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c4f3fe71-96a9-422f-af37-cbe47f62385a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034c4fb5-0c90-4d2d-b2a6-0ad3d4cc4844"],
 " below the system wires. The corrections then act from those record wires: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e0e60cc8-60cc-4909-9f32-dcb1ff6ea7bd"],
 " is an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5cfa9112-52ff-49bc-97a2-d349cc2ae881"],
 " on Bob's qubit controlled by the second record, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a51fe261-1ee0-4960-8493-b9605f4cbb8c"],
 " a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40c1e3e4-86fe-4f45-bd4a-fb9db4336301"],
 " controlled by the first, both ordinary controlled gates with a record wire \
in the control position. No classical bit ever leaves the object; the \
classical channel has become two record wires, promoted to a coherent quantum \
resource rather than removed (a record wire is a more expensive resource than \
a classical bit, not a free one)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f541814d-adee-4443-9ed0-033a0b430cee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Teleport a generic Bloch qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     FractionBox[
      StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "2"], 
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{"i", "\[Phi]"}], "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     FractionBox[
      StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "2"], 
     TemplateBox[{"1"},
      "Ket"]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9bbf77ca-25fc-44ae-900d-697a50f30a51"],
 ". The protocol succeeds if Bob ends up holding exactly the input, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Bob",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9c1a78c2-8bf4-4886-b34b-5866a64116e1"],
 ", which for a qubit means the two Bloch vectors coincide. First build the \
input state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07c7041d-37f8-4b16-ac46-6f6b1d55ff79"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "/", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[86]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"d937bfb2-2af7-48ad-90bf-76dca22cabc4"],

Cell["Read its Bloch vector:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9a504998-65c6-484e-adca-f60593ef8b2b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<BlochVector\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[87]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"f45ab3c6-f057-4d63-ae3c-e0159347e1f5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It returns the textbook ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bd58f789-09c4-4a1f-8228-c47d6b0772a2"],
 ". Now run the protocol:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d7afb0c8-1582-48f2-bb79-5737bf5d2cf8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"out", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tele", "[", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
    RowBox[{"psi", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<00\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[88]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"b3fb6266-4109-4a03-b825-afc84acd04a0"],

Cell["\<\
Read Bob's Bloch vector, the partial trace discarding Alice's two qubits and \
the two records, the four wires before Bob's:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"97934386-fbfe-4ced-98f1-3f22edc10e0e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
     RowBox[{"out", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], 
     "]"}], "[", "\"\<BlochVector\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[89]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0b4545da-aa13-4c68-b49c-8b7e65567d71"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Bob's Bloch vector returns as the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b286695-8d6a-4f15-ba4a-a8da7b509d5f"],
 ", identically in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c8c7749f-f337-48a0-9d20-e051c21425d6"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8ea3af4d-74f1-4808-8ddd-ccc6355075bd"],
 ": every pure state teleports exactly, the recovered state equals the input, \
with the classical channel carried as record wires inside the object rather \
than eliminated."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"adb091fc-a994-43d3-81f5-bebaf1f45e35"],

Cell["A coherent error, digitized and corrected", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"353a6d85-0c1c-4b40-aa38-e772311850a9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The three-qubit repetition code encodes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{"0"},
     "Ket"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{"1"},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "492779fd-4f43-4cca-b49c-7a3642cb5238"],
 " as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{"000"},
     "Ket"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{"111"},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51704935-a977-42dc-8285-6256e2261a14"],
 " and protects it against bit flips. The subtlety is that real errors are \
not discrete flips; here the error is a coherent rotation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "82146cf2-fac5-4a03-b50e-96fc30bf0b95"],
 " on the middle qubit, between no error (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eeb08e7b-4201-4b61-b09e-5b7bce76f085"],
 ") and a full flip (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fccaecb5-26d2-4e0c-b10a-4ee8b5a68367"],
 "). The founding theorem of error correction states that measuring the \
syndrome digitizes this continuous error into those two discrete cases, shown \
here symbolically."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"20f13596-d120-4aa9-a324-63d98122db8a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "First the syndrome measurement. The parity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "daf15d3a-5f36-45ce-8a01-f5db2d7b2f24"],
 " must be measured without learning anything else about the state: a \
degenerate projective measurement with two rank-two projectors ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]", 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10d39f49-cbeb-4ede-8030-68c7802ba772"],
 ", which is precisely what ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurementOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e490e610-6af5-41df-b132-94981de15b29"],
 " accepts as a list of projectors. First the single-qubit identity:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e2b03dd9-d34f-4a84-a66b-54f73068f72f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"id2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[90]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"84a8bfab-f69e-43ca-8c53-ccf5651b30ee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two-qubit parity operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d7ed017-48fc-495a-8a06-22e39f6ead83"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2736cc10-8d43-45fa-bf2f-ef4631e9ed12"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"zz", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[91]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"73e8e99e-fc88-4a43-8e13-1ec562384e73"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The syndrome measurement on a pair of qubits, the two rank-two projectors \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]", 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bfc04c92-84e1-4236-b487-a02111a33c4e"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f25f31ba-e69a-4e0c-94a5-69da2d0305ba"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"syn", "[", 
    RowBox[{"q1_", ",", " ", "q2_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
             RowBox[{"id2", ",", " ", "id2"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "zz"}], 
           ")"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"q1", ",", " ", "q2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
             RowBox[{"id2", ",", " ", "id2"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "zz"}], 
           ")"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"q1", ",", " ", "q2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"q1", ",", " ", "q2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[92]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e8e54e47-71a9-4e5e-8b6b-ce551ea7a86d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Then the full code: encode, inflict the coherent error, measure both \
parities, and decode each of the four syndrome patterns into its correction. \
The decoder is three feedforward gates with mixed polarities, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<C\>\"", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", ",", " ", "ones", ",", " ", "zeros"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32c51e3e-f7f6-4413-8ea3-964e6c3afdb5"],
 " conditions an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4831eb27-7bd1-454a-a797-002471d5ec88"],
 " on some records reading ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cfe84a88-98ee-484f-bfe8-1888cfa37526"],
 " and others reading ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5723bf04-98fd-4581-a961-41a38eb28ada"],
 ". First the encoder:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"de5e9d55-f07c-4700-a6ee-b28b6a167ad5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"enc", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", " ", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Label\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Encode\>\""}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[93]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"fdbe164c-c54d-49ab-97a1-69a4e1e9ea78"],

Cell["Then the full code, encoder through feedforward correction:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a6c79956-e303-40b2-8bc2-9495ca3eeff6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qec", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"enc", ",", "\n", "        ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<RX\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", 
     "\n", "        ", 
     RowBox[{"syn", "[", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"syn", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<C\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<C\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<C\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "3"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[94]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"9e6cf6c7-cee4-4745-926b-d45cd29be351"],

Cell["Draw it:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"061d6829-83c9-498c-8b4e-cd672f27df24"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qec", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[95]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"85fdbc4e-57e0-48cb-8a9c-291f9c108849"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The diagram lays out the whole code on five wires: the labeled ",
 Cell[BoxData["Encode"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fae76dbf-f4fb-43db-8a98-3ea7e829375a"],
 " block spreading the data qubit across the three code qubits, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ef6e362c-6964-441d-b790-0ba3b62dbec5"],
 " error on qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8d65b1fa-f9c0-428d-9528-0d0557c91b8f"],
 ", the two parity measurements placing their syndromes on record wires ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ce0ca818-fcb2-49a9-bd9f-eb132f3aa866"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cec68fa7-1126-4f55-9a6c-4f6ed5d5b49a"],
 ", and the three corrections acting from those records, each an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e03c45d8-1cd6-456e-95e1-10e41db56aca"],
 " controlled on one record and anti-controlled on the other. Run it on a \
fully symbolic data qubit:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f80f7052-4470-44ae-8c8b-0a245e06169f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"coded", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"qec", "[", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "\[Beta]"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<00\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[96]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7ebb67b9-6dd8-476a-a18b-3e91830360e5"],

Cell["\<\
Read the joint distribution of the two syndrome records, the diagonal of \
their reduced density matrix (the records sit on the first two of the five \
wires, the data on the last three):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c87058c4-e91c-462a-8e49-8797ec3f4e42"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Assuming", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Beta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Beta]", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Diagonal", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
         RowBox[{"coded", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
        "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[97]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"af13a5a3-e518-4651-b771-15e16f2e2d50"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The four syndrome weights return as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["cos",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["sin",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b00fe2f-510f-49ab-b9b3-9fe7ae2f5104"],
 ": the continuous rotation has been digitized. The code never sees a partial \
error; it sees \"no error\" with probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10d68e59-4198-41b6-9498-d624f13e2921"],
 " or \"qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "005dfdeb-e82f-4a7b-a1ea-60075f0ed81e"],
 " flipped\" with probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "87d1b633-765c-4881-937c-2bd4d887f2ad"],
 ", and the weights are independent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ff8cae3d-525d-4da8-b333-1460cb879aad"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9f43a6d8-b98b-4093-a0aa-01b7e338418c"],
 ", which is what \"measuring the syndrome without learning the state\" means."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9038dec6-eb60-469d-af7c-ed8ab9714586"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The feedforward gates then act inside each branch. The claim to check: the \
corrected state matches the ideal codeword ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{"000"},
     "Ket"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{"111"},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dab77b79-cd33-42e3-95c1-3caf5402b63e"],
 " at fidelity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b888736-46d5-49cb-a9d2-c6b977349481"],
 ", for every input and every error angle. Compute ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["F", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b0d2504-8dd1-4b5c-b79e-032f29ba0342"],
 " symbolically:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d6d505a0-08df-4fc0-a7d1-ce36ca01d8bb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Assuming", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Beta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Beta]", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumSimilarity", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
        RowBox[{"coded", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"enc", "[", 
        RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "\[Beta]"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<00\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",",
        " ", "\"\<Fidelity\>\""}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[98]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3622d770-088a-46fb-a2d6-baf4fd32946f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The fidelity returns as exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2da56903-0ed7-4b92-b481-e6a4d964b328"],
 ", for every input ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1889c90e-f3a3-410a-8718-c7e6e4e4326d"],
 " and every error angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49d603f8-24ef-4f93-8a1f-0ffc55039a49"],
 ": not a high number for one sampled case, but the digitization-of-errors \
theorem itself, obtained from the computation. (The cell fixes real \
amplitudes so the symbolic fidelity closes cleanly; the result is in fact \
independent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "126e11a9-003e-4e5c-b10d-7f98e2189f09"],
 " and remains ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5442f1ba-401b-4fd2-9670-496ad0017f56"],
 " for complex amplitudes as well.)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"da5108d0-6e9c-4d7e-a3f2-0b63a577cea7"],

Cell["Run the measurement backwards", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d2688b9a-a37b-4850-b1fc-9cbc0b033970"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Because no branch was discarded, the measurement is a reversible \
interaction, and reversible in the laboratory, not only on paper. That a \
partial measurement can be undone while its record stays coherent, before it \
irreversibly decoheres, is an experimental fact: the probabilistic reversal, \
or 'uncollapsing', of a weak measurement has been demonstrated on a \
superconducting phase qubit (Katz et al., ",
 StyleBox["Phys. Rev. Lett.", "TI"],
 ", 2008), returning the qubit to its pre-measurement state on a heralded \
subset of runs. The cell below is the deterministic idealization of that \
result: the exact left inverse ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d47cc453-42dd-4b17-b85a-748b8fbf8feb"],
 " of a projective measurement's dilation, which undoes the interaction with \
certainty rather than on a selected outcome. QF provides the underlying \
dilation as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"m", "[", "\"\<SuperOperator\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c47bf70-362d-4d6d-9f64-aca4b5a3145d"],
 ": the isometry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f3a449d0-afea-4b96-a94e-28f6902bb8db"],
 " that carries out the measurement by appending the pointer qudit, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
       TemplateBox[{
         StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
        "Ket"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], "\[CircleTimes]", 
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
      "Ket"]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8f22a8e1-0eb5-4128-8cc8-0782b563b564"],
 ", mapping the qubit's two-dimensional space into the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b78bc520-9813-4ba3-85ea-3693c28e9722"],
 " system-and-pointer space. Because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b3980dd-4bb3-412d-a7d6-b54f92e3f651"],
 " is an isometry it satisfies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "001a482d-151c-4bb2-8d2e-e6f9a54526fb"],
 ", so it has a left inverse ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed11a764-87ce-4eb5-9ad6-39df59100bfd"],
 " that removes the pointer and undoes the measurement. Define that inverse \
as a labeled operator and apply the two in sequence, measure then un-measure. \
Build the input state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"17ec39e1-9305-4689-bde6-e6579a58cc72"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "/", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[99]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"39f963f1-d034-4ba1-a811-b4085c8e9a92"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The projective measurement on qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9226bc4d-f0c2-4fef-9eaa-07a2e245d526"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3ad50c84-df61-4b88-9770-ad0ba9b4a687"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[100]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6b4b5491-c61a-4998-a531-0f58d0a93a56"],

Cell["Its dilation isometry, daggered, is the un-measurement:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7738000f-81e4-4f2c-abf8-290dd7c3f3ad"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"unmeasure", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"m", "[", "\"\<SuperOperator\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", 
     "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Label\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Un-measure\>\""}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[101]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"74290d5a-6de1-45b0-8870-e34a9fbd9f83"],

Cell["Compose the two into a measure-then-unmeasure circuit:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9c0f4b33-8010-4d16-87a5-fd77ca207492"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"backward", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"m", ",", " ", "unmeasure"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[102]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"bcf8a82b-8e6f-4988-b17d-2762d0ca0750"],

Cell["Draw it:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"738248e2-e367-42ad-8493-b4eed0664a58"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"backward", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[103]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"d8f6e690-bd5e-4d0b-ae29-9830cb302787"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The diagram is two boxes on one wire: the measurement placing its outcome \
on the pointer record, then the labeled ",
 Cell["Un-measure", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "962019c3-92ce-4a74-9bac-37f02f1f5aa5"],
 " block removing it. Apply the whole circuit to the input and read the \
resulting state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1ed790f6-75ee-422e-80a3-4eca23f87307"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"backward", "[", "psi", "]"}], "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", 
      "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[104]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"20858fc0-5943-47ff-be41-7461b552a234"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The state returns as exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     FractionBox[
      StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "2"]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{"i", "\[Phi]"}], "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     FractionBox[
      StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "2"]}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eb9ecc25-08b6-44bc-8c5d-d0ce149e8d59"],
 ", the input recovered including its phase: the measurement is undone \
exactly. A projective measurement is irreversible only once its record is \
discarded; while the record remains a wire, the interaction is reversible, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3015d5db-3bad-48da-9ef7-1e97df4c7987"],
 " exactly as von Neumann wrote it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c5ed5acf-1488-4155-b46f-d5fe669604f7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A record, then, is a wire that gates can be conditioned on, that can be \
traced out, read jointly with the system, or undone. The cost is equally \
explicit: each measurement appends a pointer qudit, so a circuit with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d4694847-b13d-4b15-8805-8211073f465a"],
 " measurements on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1bdcaaca-74d2-4366-a53d-10ad8143618a"],
 " qubits evolves a state of dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["2", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c8c89c3-494d-4a5e-8b7e-48418082a1d9"],
 ". That growth is not overhead; it is the cost of retaining every branch, \
and it is what the teleportation identity, the digitization theorem, and the \
un-measurement above rely on. Retaining every branch is one computational \
strategy among several, which leads to the next claim: QF has three."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7333330a-d3a4-42a2-b81c-15823cc5778a"],

Cell["Claim 4: One object model, three computational engines", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"833f16e2-c9d1-4d87-b5c7-e2eae7f02d54"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Key feature:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " the objects of Claims 1 through 3 never specified how they are computed. \
Underneath a circuit application are three interchangeable engines: exact \
state-vector algebra (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Schrodinger\>\""}]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9422015f-7d61-45e6-bd6f-d0b3efbeeb53"],
 "), tensor-network contraction (the default), and a compiled stabilizer \
tableau (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Stabilizer\>\""}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ab6702fb-3d3e-45b2-9fef-fbb93aa8e941"],
 "), each suited to a different regime of symbols, structure, and scale. The \
exact state-vector path is the dense baseline, a literal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55d8bd5c-2adb-4a6b-b00f-ebe580c7838a"],
 " matrix-vector product available on demand; the two engines that genuinely \
change the representation, and so deserve a closer look, are the \
tensor-network default and the stabilizer tableau, taken in turn. Because all \
three share one object model, their representations then convert into one \
another exactly."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"79dd7378-d3a2-4adb-9f4c-819241762a30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Closest competitor.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Qiskit Aer exposes the same multi-engine idea through its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"method", "="}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "df1627b3-4d44-4849-8112-dd72913fa36e"],
 " switch across nine backends with automatic selection; what QF adds beyond \
the switch is that all three representations are one symbolic object that \
interconverts exactly, plus ",
 Cell[BoxData["StabilizerFrame"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c920cf01-9d0a-477c-ade6-3be952e03c32"],
 ", an exact stabilizer-rank object that falls back automatically at the \
first non-Clifford gate and carries symbolic parameters through the tableau."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5bd46a3f-1eb7-40e6-8bd4-8cd9b672df83"],

Cell["The default engine: a steered tensor-network contraction", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"56c5b2af-6747-459b-8423-6136301ac61f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Applying a circuit is, by default, a tensor-network contraction, and the \
order of the pairwise contractions determines the cost: every step produces \
an intermediate tensor, the expense is set by the largest intermediate the \
order creates (in matrix-product language, the bond dimension it requires), \
and a poor order can be exponentially more expensive than a good one on the \
same network. QF provides that choice as a ",
 Cell[BoxData["Method"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "befd8708-7243-434b-b6a9-5b1110ada8cc"],
 " sub-option, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Path\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Greedy\>\""}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "990a4468-f075-4582-b785-325e1ec8b5dd"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Optimal\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "44f9c8ab-467b-4bbf-97c1-71ea56f6ebdd"],
 ", or an explicit list computed and inspected with ",
 Cell[BoxData["GreedyContractionPath"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8d22f380-574d-4791-9ff5-337d1f509981"],
 " / ",
 Cell[BoxData["OptimalContractionPath"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b1af5ca5-a423-4b5c-82e4-ccfc99a6ba9f"],
 ". Take a familiar algorithm: Grover's search for the single input a Boolean \
oracle accepts among ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["N", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["2", "8"], "=", "256"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f4210ac9-99f8-41c3-b69e-0fe821e9843d"],
 " candidates. The named ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<GroverPhase\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2da88539-4924-4963-8fa7-5358bc2fad24"],
 " circuit is one Grover iteration ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["O", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b425098-144a-48d2-95ad-cc2cb983f85c"],
 ", the diffusion ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5af22c8f-f460-42fe-891f-cf9b96a6a22e"],
 " after the phase oracle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["O", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c762766a-c885-463c-bdc6-cc11c6895be4"],
 "; stack the peak number of them, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftFloor]",
    SpanMaxSize->1,
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   FractionBox["\[Pi]", "4"], 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["N", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[RightFloor]",
    SpanMaxSize->1,
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], "=", "12"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "216240c4-6f3f-44eb-ad93-c20fe0ec05c8"],
 ", on the uniform superposition and contract the whole search through a \
greedily chosen path. The search register size:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"73a00528-0d79-4c5e-9c22-ef7b80615a8a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", "8"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[105]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ab43c84e-c2ab-43c5-9a9b-35fafec94913"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The marked input, the single accepted candidate among ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["2", "8"], "=", "256"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47493862-fe61-4126-b48f-d21d583c5bc8"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66206ce1-9b56-4726-b158-de98a135909d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"marked", " ", "=", " ", "200"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[106]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"326dc7f5-c2ee-4dda-b92b-e4180831f420"],

Cell["Build the Boolean oracle that accepts only that input:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4c3d4d0b-8191-4bbe-a30e-8cd50a07745e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"oracle", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BooleanFunction", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", "^", "marked"}], ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[107]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4a0809cd-0b49-44be-82f2-0ac958955bec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One Grover iteration ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["O", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c6a35b8c-e807-4114-a77d-f95c9762238b"],
 ", the diffusion after the phase oracle:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1c222fda-d577-4ec7-b1b2-c5a8febdbc8d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"step", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<GroverPhase\>\"", "[", "oracle", "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[108]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"018a8edb-5471-4f35-9517-8b89d341e56d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The peak iteration count from the exact rotation angle, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["round",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[NegativeThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   FractionBox["\[Pi]", 
    RowBox[{"4", 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fd00ca32-014a-4418-923a-d8d7571c87f5"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["arcsin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"1", "/", 
     StyleBox["N", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "823a6501-eab6-4582-b32c-c6ba8c14f039"],
 " (which is ",
 Cell[BoxData["12"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d2072c0-4ee4-4287-85bd-f4ce822a66ac"],
 " here, where the coarser ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftFloor]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["\[Pi]", "4"], 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["N", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightFloor]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54143789-e2d6-441e-aac3-f54c79021003"],
 " agrees):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dbb9f219-0b14-4514-8821-fe6668e98ca5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kopt", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Pi", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"4", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ArcSin", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{"1", "/", 
           RowBox[{"2", "^", "n"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
     
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[109]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"8566d0fe-9c9c-412d-a411-a91c0a7dc6ad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The full search: a Hadamard layer, then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2837400f-5ab9-470f-9a09-638d6c4352c5"],
 " stacked iterations:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8f4ed97b-72a3-41fa-9e24-c719d6f2c0a3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"grover", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", "n", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
      RowBox[{"step", ",", " ", "kopt"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[110]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"15039f7c-324d-40df-9f05-228cf82f73d1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Draw the flattened circuit, gate labels off since the diffusion block \
repeats ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10307d9f-0a0a-428a-9364-46579da70fd8"],
 " times:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"efa96fdf-eddf-4934-8d6a-c9df33fc059c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"grover", "[", "\"\<Flatten\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowGateLabels\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[111]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"82276853-1035-44a6-b0ad-85dd065175c5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Apply it to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{"0", "\[Ellipsis]", "0"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a9f689e3-5676-42c6-9913-b6f5c21a5bc9"],
 " through a greedily chosen contraction path:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"23fbccdc-951d-4260-af06-e60cdf32ec75"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"found", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"grover", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<TensorNetwork\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Path\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Greedy\>\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[112]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"936d8670-ed1b-4cf2-8299-3b3fc443905b"],

Cell["Read the largest outcome probability:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"02599131-0998-4161-8d6d-537f3d7e6670"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"found", "[", "\"\<Probabilities\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[113]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"df5c29da-bad8-44e1-86ba-c84612a78aa4"],

Cell["\<\
Because the contraction stayed exact, the probability comes back as an exact \
rational, a ratio of large integers. Read it as a decimal:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dd13e435-31f1-4240-bc81-bf94195db647"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"%", " ", "//", " ", "N"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[114]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2ade1f2c-d8ff-479d-befc-2559a73f77f7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The success probability is very close to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "94166b03-730d-4b7e-897b-8c12496f0c5f"],
 ", at the analytic Grover peak ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["arcsin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"1", "/", 
     StyleBox["N", "TI"]}]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d396110d-f298-4a98-831c-f560b23715fe"],
 " that the iteration count ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "12"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c7db348-01a8-46c4-a263-3baab507ab50"],
 " is chosen to reach; the most probable bitstring is the marked input \
itself, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"200", "=", "11001000"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9ed908ac-34c2-4b26-bfca-becb352b9040"],
 " (verified). A search of a few hundred gates, contracted in one steered \
pass."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7d060d49-a27b-4060-ad58-d4ccafa3c1b1"],

Cell["\<\
The contraction plan is itself an inspectable object. Extract the circuit's \
tensor network:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b7f18054-ad8c-42f8-bae0-d0955b2279d6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"net", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"grover", "[", "\"\<TensorNetwork\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[115]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"b2c7ab9c-7aac-4ab0-8f17-3edea3e420ba"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the greedy path and draw it as a tree, its branching the order in \
which the network is folded together:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"716a18cc-047c-4ac0-96f5-51198e98fc4f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ContractionTree", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"TensorNetworkContraction", "[", 
    RowBox[{"net", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"GreedyContractionPath", "[", "net", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TreeElementLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"All", " ", "->", " ", "None"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TreeElementShapeFunction", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"All", " ", "->", " ", "None"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[116]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"18228c2f-2c89-4f28-bc15-cad29bb33755"],

Cell["\<\
The tree is the contraction schedule: the leaves are the circuit's gate and \
state tensors, every internal node is one pairwise contraction, and the \
branching structure is the order the greedy path chose, showing which \
contractions are nested. The depth and balance of that tree are what the path \
adjusts to keep each intermediate tensor small.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a41912cb-fa57-4214-ad93-f80ad0dc3cb1"],

Cell["The stabilizer engine: the state as its symmetry group", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"c78106cf-c6e6-4daf-9c2a-c2609a8941fd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For Clifford circuits there is a representation that does not use \
amplitudes: store the state as the group of Pauli operators that fix it, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], ":", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
       "Ket"]}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{"+", 
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
      "Ket"]}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7cda5b00-e62b-4d35-9ba8-414c4e23cbe2"],
 ", whose ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8776ea5f-f6d9-41b6-ac3c-437e77df4215"],
 " commuting generators determine the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f6cd6c3c-377b-4944-a779-7646f72ef76f"],
 "-qubit state uniquely and fit in a binary symplectic tableau. This is the \
Gottesman-Knill representation, in which a Clifford gate is a constant-size \
rewrite of the tableau rather than a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "\[Times]", 
   SuperscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d7703792-ce0c-4f9e-b32e-0cf17f209f1f"],
 " matrix product. The engine is selected by one option. Build a five-qubit \
linear cluster state, the entangled resource behind measurement-based \
computing, as a layer of Hadamards followed by nearest-neighbor controlled-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "871435d4-4d31-44c9-8224-cde1b24b855a"],
 " gates:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15a2f08e-d78d-49f9-ab6f-51d8dbc636c6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"cluster5", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", "5", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[117]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"56db63d3-23b7-41c1-9af5-79faa0c7413c"],

Cell["Draw the circuit:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"786b8a54-2457-4782-989d-920c22164a65"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"cluster5", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[118]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1ba18eba-9e16-42ef-b50d-d3c8d81d1c35"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The diagram is an ordinary gate-model circuit: a Hadamard on every wire, \
then controlled-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f49b0e48-8395-453d-8a26-8d7991d2a86f"],
 " gates down the chain ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c9e89bad-1a55-4eff-be0a-dc8f18fe4a2e"],
 "-",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e1b0ec8e-17d9-4116-81f7-741bb95f43fe"],
 "-",
 Cell[BoxData["3"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "132f7fc9-e140-4bf0-8109-2e4b1d96c43d"],
 "-",
 Cell[BoxData["4"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71eb479c-94b9-493f-b5f0-356ed86dbafb"],
 "-",
 Cell[BoxData["5"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d6749472-1193-4927-a17d-3dab00d8e77b"],
 ". Nothing about it is stabilizer-specific yet; the engine is a choice made \
at application time."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c5732b56-2460-4d8c-adb1-a4cd10819e7a"],

Cell["Apply it with the stabilizer engine instead of the default:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c6d0326a-0616-401c-aa72-625a6bad854b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"stab5", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"cluster5", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Stabilizer\>\""}], "]"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[119]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"d82f9329-53dd-4352-8214-474a6f333dfe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A purely Clifford circuit that would otherwise carry a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["2", "5"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fde740d2-0715-44f9-bc5a-e162e1236069"],
 " amplitude vector returns instead a ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliStabilizer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47040d74-5480-4da6-893c-5ef89447ab8b"],
 ": the state stored as its symmetry group, not as its amplitudes."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ee468d77-b2b8-468b-9154-c4defa655ae3"],

Cell["Read the generators of that group:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8986b039-9eb6-4cb8-a347-aa4612d79493"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"stab5", "[", "\"\<PauliForm\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[120]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7c3dcfd5-9b2c-45f6-9f2c-ff6f77a7ea25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Five Pauli strings that determine the state completely. They are exactly \
the cluster-state generators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"]], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["w", "TI"], "\[Tilde]", 
     StyleBox["v", "TI"]}],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["w", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16bffde2-b31b-4c17-b8a4-057ff11f3777"],
 " along the chain, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "734b3f1c-98fe-472d-8b64-1bd9cd2c5928"],
 " on each site flanked by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bbdb1097-5207-49ca-ae59-b4baf950a123"],
 " on its neighbors."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"592d0fe3-652a-4e70-8b07-2e2e0e9a040c"],

Cell["\<\
Pauli expectations are closed-form algebra on the generators, with no state \
vector anywhere:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b373a3dd-63ba-401c-8e5a-d967ef9933ba"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<XZIII\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"stab5", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Expectation\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<XZIII\>\""}], "]"}]}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<IZXZI\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"stab5", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Expectation\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<IZXZI\>\""}], "]"}]}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<XXIII\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"stab5", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Expectation\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<XXIII\>\""}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "|>"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[121]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"dd41d8a2-1257-4fe6-ace3-1c32ed1ed525"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two generators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8266f8df-59d8-4dfc-8075-4d5b0d68374a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "3"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40ba6823-149f-44ed-9619-f0537d72e0f1"],
 " return deterministically ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e1ebdfdc-140a-4395-86aa-c03870501346"],
 ", while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"X", "X"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6760c86f-b194-4802-a64d-7a2e9a565ef0"],
 " on the first two sites, which anticommutes with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "1"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21620b05-fef7-49af-a84b-e1c4cdcdbeb7"],
 ", is exactly unbiased, all read off by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\|01d53d", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38285b27-89f7-458e-b53f-149d5cb73569"],
 " phase tracking."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6d8c088e-24ef-40f8-8fd3-b8e192929d58"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The advantage of the representation is scale. Apply twenty thousand random \
Clifford gates to a thousand qubits, a state whose amplitude vector would \
need ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["2", "1000"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09fcacdb-9951-4245-ae60-c8e7965f908e"],
 " entries. The qubit count:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"46e8dcfc-5fb8-42f7-88ce-6e01168dafa0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", "1000"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[122]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"d206f2a4-1cc9-4c88-b226-324c70bdbffb"],

Cell["\<\
Build the random gate stream, twenty thousand Hadamard, CNOT, and phase gates \
(seeded for reproducibility):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3c6dfc4f-d8c7-4220-9d75-b8875135d6e3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "1", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gates", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"RandomInteger", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"RandomSample", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", "n", "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"RandomInteger", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "6666", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[123]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2f796300-fe46-4b6b-8d57-bf037040548b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Apply them to the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de61c54-7170-4690-8993-e637594a4226"],
 "-qubit stabilizer state and time the evolution:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b4ac27fb-0e01-4169-9fa5-79ce1b60edce"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"First", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"big", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", "n", "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<ApplyCircuit\>\"", ",", " ", "gates"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[124]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a7dd4478-1291-44a8-81c0-ae7da0ceeb5f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The whole gate stream folds in a fraction of a second: ",
 Cell[BoxData["ApplyCircuit"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8f5ca208-b9ac-40ef-844c-7fe6dd0d6fea"],
 " runs the tableau updates through one compiled kernel whose per-gate cost \
is flat in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9d8a0b85-e798-46eb-aff7-75fca2c596df"],
 " and independent of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b2968e81-b56e-4a34-9e63-3e3577c49999"],
 " that never gets built. The cross-engine comparison is boundary-dependent \
rather than a single ratio: a dedicated C++ tableau (Stim) is roughly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", "\[Times]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b598d78e-4ddb-4c9a-9133-aec56b33d327"],
 " faster at the engine core and ",
 Cell[BoxData["11"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7504757-23e4-41da-9409-aa185ac903d1"],
 "-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"16", "\[Times]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4eece96e-33f5-482a-819a-cc6b01dc81a9"],
 " faster end to end, while a Python-driven gate-by-gate pipeline around that \
same C++ engine is about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"27", "\[Times]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9cf45b-f468-4318-a8f4-15189cecd4c6"],
 " slower than this one compiled call (measurements in the companion ",
 Cell["QF-Stabilizer-vs-Packages.md", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "e85a59c1-1150-43dc-a549-de4da27f45d9"],
 "). The bipartite entanglement entropy across the half-chain cut is then a \
closed form, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["rank",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    SubscriptBox["\|01d53d", "2"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{
     "generators", "\[NonBreakingSpace]", "restricted", "\[NonBreakingSpace]",
       "to", "\[NonBreakingSpace]"}],
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["A", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f93a27be-62bb-4642-80cc-6318b51da2c0"],
 ", exact at any qubit count:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cbcddeb3-2d70-4133-a2e9-2911a4fc7cff"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"big", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Entropy\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[125]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"69afd67c-93f4-438c-b489-111ff5679b3a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The entropy returns just below its half-chain maximum: the random circuit \
has driven the chain to near-maximal, Page-like entanglement, and whatever \
gate sequence the sampler draws, the value is an exact integer from an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\|01d53d", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7de6eb46-e464-4567-99eb-f737a9fce4c4"],
 " rank, not an estimate. The boundary of the formalism is handled directly \
as well: a non-Clifford gate (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f6a82e99-b6ee-4a72-8c1b-4e7ad60eae57"],
 ", or a general phase) steps outside the stabilizer group, and QF returns a ",
 Cell[BoxData["StabilizerFrame"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d46764e-32f2-49c7-8db8-d95aa9f6eccb"],
 ", a superposition of stabilizer states, rather than a wrong answer."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"df3b2a25-6d15-4b6e-80ec-21a11edfd430"],

Cell["The representations convert exactly", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"90ff57c4-0e98-49ad-acb0-6f9e90e36eb2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The engines are not separate; one object model means the representations \
interconvert. Start from an ordinary three-qubit linear cluster circuit, a \
Hadamard on every wire followed by two nearest-neighbor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"C", "Z"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f654b53-161b-4e2c-9e5d-40db247c6547"],
 " bonds:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b3e1597-6952-49e9-b7ca-48483fc9c4cf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"cluster3", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", "3", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "\"\<CZ\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[126]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c4a41c14-44ea-45c1-8db7-7681c5877b01"],

Cell["Draw it:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c7cba421-fdae-4722-a689-993aabb065a4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"cluster3", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[127]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"36b0e23f-43d0-4468-b476-fc350d5217e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bare ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<CZ\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60c395b7-e335-463e-b8ae-c5a0d13143b9"],
 " acts on the default first pair and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2700b8f3-ecf7-42e4-8cd0-61c93fa795e5"],
 " on the next, so the diagram shows the bond chain ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
  "1", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", "-", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", "2", 
   "\[NegativeThinSpace]", "-", "\[NegativeThinSpace]", "3"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2339b289-ad37-43ef-98cb-1b65c0029b23"],
 ": nothing here is stabilizer-specific, only gates."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b314f26-da08-4d52-8cdd-5e75d46d1d7d"],

Cell["\<\
Apply that same circuit through the stabilizer engine, which stores the state \
as its symmetry group rather than its amplitudes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ac50f22c-d97f-4849-aa8c-65d68c946a10"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"stab3", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"cluster3", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Stabilizer\>\""}], "]"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[128]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c68034da-23d3-4a4a-a786-bf9aaaaa21dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliStabilizer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a8783b05-24a1-4802-aa3c-22170929b767"],
 " returns, the state held as the three cluster generators that fix it. Now \
expand that tableau back into an exact state, that is, solve ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "df923c19-c2ff-4095-8f8b-4da9bbe23167"],
 " for the unique joint ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "88641245-601c-40dc-8af1-2723ad56eca9"],
 " eigenstate of the three generators:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"342c12cf-6edb-4a31-86ed-c1fcd10fca16"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "stab3", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "TraditionalForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[129]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ade5362b-8191-4172-bec9-8eb6908b1851"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ket returns as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", 
    SqrtBox["8"]], 
   RowBox[{
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "3"]}]], 
     TemplateBox[{
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "3"]}]},
      "Ket"]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "af0c129c-3122-42ea-822d-a24146ae051e"],
 ": a uniform superposition over all eight bitstrings whose sign is fixed by \
the two cluster bonds, negative exactly on ",
 Cell[BoxData["011"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "506ecc89-5056-42e4-86e0-e1b77cb6b0f0"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["110"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ca8ac30e-6895-4f87-bb78-222a68ba1fb2"],
 ", the tableau expanded into exact amplitudes. The agreement with the \
default engine is not approximate; check it with ",
 Cell[BoxData["SameQ"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e0880335-8285-4104-a34c-1c5972be58b8"],
 ", the language's structural identity:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bef0e96f-5653-4d39-ad4d-fd4344094bd7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "stab3", "]"}], "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", 
   "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"cluster3", "[", "]"}], "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[130]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"fcefedb6-593e-498d-803e-41a9f73a65c2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "830cb050-40bb-4bdb-8e4c-90bf4ea70ce3"],
 ": the two engines produced the same exact expression, global phase included."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"03ef7035-7265-4f4e-94eb-ed7e7de9a46e"],

Cell["\<\
The conversion also runs back to circuits: the tableau synthesizes a Clifford \
circuit that prepares it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f82972f7-358c-4238-a245-d462f3cccd12"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"stab3", "[", "\"\<Circuit\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[131]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3a585578-6f3a-428c-98a8-86c7c373a199"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A five-gate Clifford circuit returns, interleaved Hadamards and \
controlled-NOTs, and applying it to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"000"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b101b63e-2924-424e-a5d2-df5c0e9cfafb"],
 " reproduces the state vector exactly (verified). Circuit to tableau, \
tableau to state, tableau back to circuit: three representations of one \
object, each available where it is cheapest, with symbols, structure, or \
scale deciding which engine runs."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bd9eaa9c-b00a-45d6-a4e2-958b223888be"],

Cell["\<\
Claim 5: A quantum object is an ordinary Wolfram Language expression\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ad06276f-ba0f-4711-9647-a3f55d6ebf9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Key feature:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " this is what underlies everything above, the reason Claim 1's algebra is \
symbolic and Claim 4's three engines share one model: a QF object is a \
symbolic expression like any other in the language, so the kernel's own \
functions operate on the object and return another object. ",
 Cell[BoxData["Exp"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71ab5255-aa20-4875-abf6-6b87d0a74494"],
 " exponentiates a generator into a propagator, ",
 Cell[BoxData["D"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "44882817-1ab5-4de4-8df4-0aaa8f229c3c"],
 " differentiates a parametrized gate into another operator, ",
 Cell[BoxData["Plus"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ee79aab-7118-429a-93ba-9cb225c297dd"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["Commutator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a74b3447-6266-46c5-af7d-528d884a1c31"],
 " build a Hamiltonian from named Paulis, and the closed-form scalars these \
objects yield pass into solvers like ",
 Cell[BoxData["Maximize"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40d7cd24-df7e-4778-8108-c739f050860b"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["Reduce"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c2269907-8283-45c0-b8d2-1776adff43ec"],
 ". Nothing is converted, extracted, or exported first: the same ",
 Cell[BoxData["Exp"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4981afc2-a668-4f2b-8515-f57d89659e6d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["D"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ef0915ab-0782-4735-bd97-8fc21fbfa639"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["Plus"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ff40ae9d-2108-4b92-8478-7bcbf3a92f1f"],
 " one would call on a number-matrix act unchanged on a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c1526c9d-5ddb-449d-a236-9c4093719fc8"],
 " and return a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c57bb5e-50ba-47de-aa41-e964ae6fb8c4"],
 ". The overload set is real but finite, ",
 Cell[BoxData["Exp"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "017815c8-b70d-4c51-bd10-1f5a68e85d7e"],
 " (and ",
 Cell[BoxData["MatrixExp"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ce5885bd-d84f-42fd-ad54-bd0de4bd812a"],
 "), ",
 Cell[BoxData["D"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "751062bc-e3a1-4443-b4f3-1fd52ad9db6d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["Plus"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ce8aa377-aa80-4dad-a1c9-4bedb59213ab"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["Times"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e74f79e-d406-4488-aa73-6434554be076"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["Power"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e42376b5-32d0-45a8-87d2-2f127d085dc5"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["Tr"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06676c6e-08a2-4dba-8066-041f685cedca"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["Commutator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "885902d5-212f-483b-b7c8-07ee32e0ab36"],
 " and the analytic functions act on operators; for ",
 Cell[BoxData["Eigenvalues"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "de3903f4-a949-41e6-9620-455b9d9f6750"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData["Det"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bb435df-187d-4e89-afff-88bb9691af0b"],
 " one still reaches through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"obj", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bb65cce-c385-46fb-b053-7b2a555f1327"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cf3e2eff-17a7-45d3-a88e-b7e40a12cbb1"],

Cell["Superposition by native arithmetic", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"45088449-fd09-4a12-8457-898f470cd420"],

Cell["\<\
Write a state as a sum of kets scaled by amplitudes, and check it against the \
named one:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c3dd61ce-7930-48ae-adf3-1104745b6b84"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<1\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<+\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[132]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"164aa124-01fc-4992-8539-5d1f7ef5f4c0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The comparison returns ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b44a1b35-8f28-4838-a88c-a57f3ecc3a9a"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData["Plus"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f5210ec-5203-4005-9509-16d4442c20b1"],
 " and the scalar division act on the state objects, assembling ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     TemplateBox[{"1"},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8a267951-8067-4ddb-ad71-32a49c8887b2"],
 " as a genuine ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bb8291f2-13c8-400f-9c65-10c02741b3f9"],
 ", and QF's overloaded ",
 Cell[BoxData["=="], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9c6858fd-6d81-4497-be26-647b39c47eb4"],
 " confirms it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29c62357-e971-4a21-b9c3-e73863b27bf6"],
 ". No amplitudes were extracted by hand, and the same arithmetic extends to \
the more substantial overloads below."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9a5adfee-e460-4083-9731-41be553eddd8"],

Cell["The exponential map: a generator becomes a propagator", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"254964ea-6c4d-465d-90a7-f9aa3d392181"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The propagator of a Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ee50ea8-6179-4b36-aae3-41a5dc5ba5f3"],
 " is the matrix exponential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5963daa0-9c72-4517-9f1e-a417d1006d48"],
 ". Write it directly, with the kernel's ",
 Cell[BoxData["Exp"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b87a295d-7b45-40f6-ae11-2adac03b72dd"],
 " acting on the generator object:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ec7917ed-a820-489d-9943-63162740a441"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"uexp", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "t"}], ")"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[133]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6839b7d2-ed1c-43b2-81d1-e72d70aeeee5"],

Cell["Read its label and its matrix (trig-simplified):", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"34895cec-782e-4ccf-8d49-2d77a7e1ec09"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"uexp", "[", "\"\<Label\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "@", 
    RowBox[{"FullSimplify", " ", "@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ExpToTrig", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Normal", " ", "@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"uexp", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}]}]}]}]}]}], "}"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[134]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4bc214f5-b741-418b-9567-bbd1484dad41"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is a new ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "df7cdee2-dcef-4874-9603-47453c6b1a08"],
 " whose label reads ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ecc0560-f795-4d88-b557-970b663b4409"],
 " and whose matrix is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9777d677-e269-400f-bd0d-a7f5c155a341"],
 "-rotation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["cos",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["sin",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]},
     {
      RowBox[{"-", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["sin",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["cos",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]}
    }], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f2a9e3b-25f4-4d6a-8c17-8840e27378be"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData["Exp"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a35096c1-8068-4662-9f80-6578a0b7e59c"],
 " performed a genuine matrix exponential on the operator, mixing the two \
levels through the off-diagonal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a08434e0-04d3-4e40-8d2b-eabbfe4cb718"],
 " rather than exponentiating entries one by one, and the generator was never \
reduced to a number-matrix first. (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", "...", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fdc16ae9-9f2c-47ba-ada7-8d555d73f445"],
 " returns the identical operator.)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8fa32104-879d-431b-9083-1976d8762322"],

Cell["Operator algebra in one line", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"073c4ea8-5404-4f6c-8b18-eccda9ea24af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ordinary ",
 Cell[BoxData["Plus"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "631de661-3091-4478-8f76-37f73e1f96d5"],
 " and scalar multiplication assemble a Hamiltonian on the object, and the \
Pauli decomposition reads the coefficients back out:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3dbbb659-b996-45dd-b6b9-b0132b619b9d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hab", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"a", " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
   RowBox[{"b", " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[135]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"f2caea67-a5f5-4970-a8b8-1cba75d68947"],

Cell["Read its label and its Pauli decomposition:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6f6e9e01-ce12-401f-a726-53434f717b6e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"hab", "[", "\"\<Label\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"hab", "[", "\"\<PauliDecompose\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[136]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4f9483ca-591d-49d2-8ce7-020ecd50cdcb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The operator carries the label ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e9ac53a1-6213-45f1-aed1-23d5354032c9"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"hab", "[", "\"\<PauliDecompose\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e75727bb-eb3a-46a9-a5f4-5ebd9f6f0b63"],
 " returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"<|", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"X", " ", "->", " ", "a"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Z", " ", "->", " ", "b"}]}], "|>"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25e0a7ad-471e-4442-8fc1-4e07ddf0ba02"],
 ": a round-trip through the algebra, coefficients in by arithmetic and back \
out by decomposition, on a symbolic operator rather than a numeric lookup \
table. The algebra goes beyond arithmetic. The kernel's ",
 Cell[BoxData["Commutator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "24b89c85-6dd5-46cd-87a0-c6a04f6cdc80"],
 " gives the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "2", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f7a9b2ba-5ee6-44c8-8d84-cd7e7753f7eb"],
 " relation as an operator identity:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"27ebfcda-08df-4204-b93d-0ccdda3b556c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Commutator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Y\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"2", " ", "I", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[137]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"996e802c-3d56-4010-abf9-56d0dd5dbce3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2efab3ae-e743-4e74-9a1d-5d30a45e85f2"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5fc46f48-6ea9-440f-acda-ac5a6ce2ecba"],
 ", computed on the operators and verified against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "da66c1e0-25c9-438f-8c4c-697dd6bbe321"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b455989-029d-4b25-b55f-322ee6e0e3e5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Operator calculus: recover ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d0c5b18-3296-4aba-bc62-63599b866572"],
 " from a target ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2df561ee-ddb0-41ca-80cf-d0b60c179d36"]
}], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"cd95fdf2-9b7a-41cc-947a-33c93cdd01b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Claim 1 solved Hamiltonians forward into their propagators; the inverse is \
pure operator calculus. Choose a unitary trajectory ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "98dc8ab2-2c95-451e-b371-e385ee2fd171"],
 ", and the Hamiltonian that drives it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], " ", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], "."], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fb03041c-8cd6-4b05-93ed-796e135a6090"],
 ", the basis of counterdiabatic driving and shortcuts to adiabaticity. \
Compose the target ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "376982b5-976b-47d2-a6dd-365712b256a3"],
 " from named gates:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"03cdcd96-f6d9-4830-b70a-8d6fcb14b7ff"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"utgt", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<RZ\>\"", "[", 
     RowBox[{"t", "^", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<RX\>\"", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[138]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"cb39dfff-92c1-40b3-8903-6a6ff295f79b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Differentiate it as an operator with the kernel's ",
 Cell[BoxData["D"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16d9a170-5aeb-40ab-90c7-ba5e4f9ff007"],
 " and close it with the operator's own ",
 Cell[BoxData["Dagger"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b95fe325-188d-4e42-ba65-e142c127aa47"],
 ", forming ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], " ", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], "."], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73952867-de38-4794-9db2-0cc720e206a5"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d900c922-8555-4ae4-b5f3-21d895f4cf7b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hdrive", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"I", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"D", "[", 
     RowBox[{"utgt", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"utgt", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[139]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c94fe028-8fc2-4c44-bd9c-a82315bcfc43"],

Cell["Read the control field off each axis:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0f148661-3e01-4fe5-80ad-85f3d6a67270"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"hdrive", "[", "\"\<PauliDecompose\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[140]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3ed609c1-0ed7-4b82-8634-ab31fd62acd0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The controls return axis by axis as the drive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "+", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bcb6c974-7f00-4bb3-858e-52dae3769ace"],
 ", with a vanishing identity component, traceless as a control should be. ",
 Cell[BoxData["D"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c46df608-e0e4-4d4e-b210-c5e4933ccb4e"],
 " operated on the ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8078acf5-43eb-4487-95d5-a80e636d8d27"],
 " and returned a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "84e49e0a-8bba-4ccf-82f5-349e71d7a79b"],
 " (not a bare matrix), and composition ",
 Cell[BoxData["@"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c62e5c5e-8066-492a-bee0-d6a8fd83d55a"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["Dagger"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a6a65920-0334-4070-b5b7-4fa3b6e8783c"],
 ", and the Pauli decomposition all act on the same object; the defining \
identity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], " ", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], "."], "=", 
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["U", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "446f162e-d050-47a8-ac5a-aa4586d1311d"],
 " holds identically. The textbook inverse-design formula runs on the \
operator itself, with no differential solver involved."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7d2733e5-ed62-431f-bd04-d4411fce627d"],

Cell["Calculus on states too", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"edf1f6bd-d6cd-4fcd-81cc-4cc8893864c5"],

Cell["\<\
The derivative overload is not operator-only. Take a state whose amplitudes \
are functions of time. Build it:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6a29e65f-b42b-4e9d-a60c-8481af86f128"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[141]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"b28e77f4-789e-4fae-ae80-42c711f2bb15"],

Cell["Differentiate it twice in place and add it back:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fe905012-5495-4f04-9c03-ff2de8ad6ef4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"D", "[", 
      RowBox[{"psi", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
     "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "//", " ",
   "Normal"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[142]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"548922c8-9737-4472-b1c9-8bc748144c46"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The sum collapses to the zero vector: the object satisfies the harmonic \
identity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "\[DoublePrime]"]},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a84d23ba-e2ec-4e44-9621-fecd80fbb660"],
 " through WL's own calculus, the second derivative taken on the ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5930e1b9-62a0-48d7-8136-322f6864127e"],
 " directly."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"026a06d8-0cff-41cf-b02c-1bebb8360638"],

Cell["The scalars flow into solvers", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"a5eabd6f-3521-4256-a900-98e62916595c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "When a QF object yields a symbolic scalar, the language's solvers take \
over. The expectation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a23fdcd2-a2b6-437d-afeb-6e6f368d5d05"],
 " in the trial state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"]], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b279c7c7-5ba0-43d5-8b3f-ea0409fc7015"],
 " is a closed form. Build the trial state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d08cf75e-643d-4e56-bf93-e9941bf9bc60"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<RY\>\"", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[143]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"eb085fbd-7e27-4099-8086-d9d3357b10de"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Form the energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Bra"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "+", 
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "83e201f7-3379-40da-a089-c31f3645dfdb"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6ed05ea9-2467-4e4b-b7f5-66e5c797d98d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"energy", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", 
       RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
           
           RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}], "[", 
         "psi", "]"}], ")"}], "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[144]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2b51dcc0-83a6-4ddb-90ff-58a191de805e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Pass it to ",
 Cell[BoxData["Maximize"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "778d386e-1e61-4360-a39f-b1293925d41c"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2a7b2fd8-df60-4468-867e-a6119b79a902"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Assuming", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Maximize", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"energy", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Theta]", " ", "<=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "]"}], 
    " ", "//", " ", "FullSimplify"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[145]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2071c2d3-d7b9-4ad8-bbaa-2f86b1fa58d2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The energy is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d34aa52d-a54a-4e58-91fa-fb0462264fde"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData["Maximize"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "451c0985-c8c2-4660-94d0-6f457b19faf3"],
 " returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox["2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b18d503e-8ff4-4409-b8c2-c0539fef0178"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c0afce95-b54b-4b55-ae28-be5cfd026251"],
 ": the exact extremal value, recognizable as the operator norm of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "547f2629-cf91-4803-b77a-91a9c1f9fd97"],
 ", a complete variational eigenvalue calculation done by composing objects \
with native arithmetic and optimization. The same approach certifies a \
physical threshold. The Werner state's realignment criterion, a quantity \
positive exactly when it witnesses entanglement, is a symbolic function of \
the mixing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "301a1fcc-9ad2-42f7-90ef-a8c6e95c2098"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ef0cb87b-a8e8-49ab-85c3-584842a15ade"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"crit", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumEntanglementMonotone", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Werner\>\"", "[", 
         RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
       " ", "\"\<Realignment\>\""}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "p", " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[146]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e1f35e98-74f2-49a0-b010-fb27a5321805"],

Cell["Turn the criterion into the exact entanglement threshold:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"48a4924a-b9a0-49a6-887e-34eda591215e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Reduce", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"crit", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "p", " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}], ",", " ", "p"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[147]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"62bdbef8-6543-4cd5-bc1f-db65983d3b41"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The criterion is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox[
   RowBox[{GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{"3", "-", "4", 
        StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "-", "1"}], "2"]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51ba6154-d534-4613-a81f-9cf0dcb2d45b"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData["Reduce"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dd052146-d6e2-4bb1-875a-2883ba5ba8e2"],
 " turns it into the exact threshold: the Werner state is entangled precisely \
for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "<", 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "<", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "389bce86-b4fa-4cad-af7d-6460a26cda00"],
 ", a physical fact certified by passing a QF-derived expression to a native \
solver."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dd101d69-f51a-4a6b-b4bd-aaf52675fb77"],

Cell["Claim 6: Every object draws itself", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"37e8bdbf-773d-452e-b56e-2b8176aff1cc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Key feature:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Claim 5 let the kernel's functions read an object; here the object draws \
itself. Visualization is property dispatch, not a separate plotting library: \
each object provides plot properties that render through the Wolfram Language \
graphics system and forward its options, so a publication figure is one call \
on the object it depicts. The set of views is wide. States draw as Bloch \
vectors, amplitude and probability charts, and qudit pie and sector wheels; \
measurements as outcome histograms; stabilizer states as their binary \
symplectic tableau; circuits as gate diagrams, tensor-network graphs, and \
multiway and causal views. Adiabatic evolutions add spectrum, gap, and \
coupling plots (in the ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOptimization"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65136664-f109-4fd8-8429-8b773a49b0a3"],
 " sub-package), the underlying ",
 Cell[BoxData["TensorNetwork"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c8dbd622-efb2-4443-9642-e9074d94cca6"],
 " renders as a hypergraph through the TensorNetworks paclet, and the \
phase-space objects of Claim 2 plot as Wigner surfaces. Below, one example \
per object kind."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aeebdaf9-4850-4a91-b1bf-92320d6e2b00"],

Cell["A state on the Bloch sphere", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"73552895-274b-4554-b68f-abae382bcd15"],

Cell["A single qubit draws its own Bloch vector:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"004d265d-1fc2-4df7-815f-230dd4619beb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "5"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "5"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "3"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], 
  "[", "\"\<BlochPlot\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[148]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"ef2c7046-a09a-4d11-a022-ef4ab4a7373c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The output is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["Graphics3D"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "85aec044-35c4-447e-b4ba-4aa6b81b3292"],
 " of the sphere with the state's arrow at polar angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", "/", "5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00bbe786-25ca-40fc-91e8-e4cc6571bc92"],
 " and azimuth ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "995e1f4a-f012-452d-b85e-f4002fe2e3d4"],
 ": the geometry of the state, drawn by the state."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26907e46-7b18-4482-b1fa-4edc85d98874"],

Cell["Amplitudes that keep their phases", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5c9a80c4-8f67-4133-9f5d-f9487a93969b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A bar chart of probabilities discards the phases; ",
 Cell[BoxData["AmplitudesChart"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d8057f7-e754-466d-a9f6-28de97843465"],
 " draws the complex amplitudes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "BraKet"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25adce5d-4f38-457b-93c6-f21493e187fc"],
 " themselves, heights for the magnitudes ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4628ed15-285b-483a-bd7b-61d298744887"],
 " and colors for the phases ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["arg",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65edd7ce-c91c-4c32-b887-8e7eae2d36c0"],
 ". Apply a quantum Fourier transform to the two-term superposition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", 
    SqrtBox["2"]], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"000"},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     TemplateBox[{"101"},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9df3756d-a86b-4034-b218-74989b8c3655"],
 ", which the transform spreads into a phase-rich pattern across all eight \
basis states:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ee8cbedc-ac47-424c-9a37-14b3226eb9f5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Fourier\>\"", "[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", 
       " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<AmplitudesChart\>\"", ",", " ", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ChartLegends", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "3"}]}], ",", " ", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"Automatic", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[149]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"20d03956-b556-4467-b327-7633bd457b96"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The eight bars return with magnitudes tracing an interference comb, a clean \
null at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"100"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e6d2fb29-f091-4b6a-8d1e-dd0e2d43712a"],
 ", and the surviving bars tinted by a wheel of distinct phase colors keyed \
by the legend: the QFT's phase ramp made visible alongside the magnitudes, \
the full complex state in one figure."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"932c4c69-232b-4969-9307-aa8c7db5b4ce"],

Cell["A measurement draws its statistics", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"0d9a9c34-60ae-4969-a2bc-c01b78f25418"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19ee51f1-a06b-44d2-9948-0e2fe0b4b46e"],
 " object charts its own outcome distribution, the Born probabilities ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       TemplateBox[{
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
        "BraKet"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bc61e104-380e-4eb1-93f7-7fe474f8d232"],
 ". Run the Bernstein-Vazirani circuit for a hidden string ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "=", "1011"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "86e06fa4-1d81-40c1-8391-51f13f82d19d"],
 ", a single oracle query that encodes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "88e4d572-fcaf-447e-a333-a599bc78d193"],
 " in the interference pattern, and let it draw the statistics of its own \
final measurement:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7638f302-39aa-4805-869e-44c824970862"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<BernsteinVazirani\>\"", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], 
     "]"}], "]"}], "[", "]"}], "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<ProbabilitiesPlot\>\"", ",", " ", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<LabelsAngle\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"90", " ", "Degree"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "3"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[150]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"83aedfa2-bd08-49cf-95bb-5121f059fc53"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The histogram collapses to a single bar of height ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b27c809-80e0-4692-a9fa-7fbff90c4afd"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData["1011"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d69e73f-7e59-4cdc-a6db-ee544550caa4"],
 ", every other outcome exactly zero: one query has extracted the entire \
hidden string from the Born statistics, the deterministic signature of the \
algorithm. The hardware result in Claim 7 is the same kind of object, which \
is why simulated and measured statistics compare so directly there."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"31a7b04f-62c4-49a4-a936-8ca329192066"],

Cell["A stabilizer state shows its tableau", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"958dbe69-f0ac-461f-9507-083f35d8806f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The stabilizer states of Claim 4 have a native picture of their own: the \
binary symplectic tableau, the actual data structure the formalism computes \
on. Feed the five-cycle graph ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], "5"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a86b7c2b-ea1c-4425-8148-d3ae708f7138"],
 " straight into ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliStabilizer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7ad33ee-7fc6-48b1-98bf-abe01aac3c20"],
 " to build its ring cluster state, and draw the tableau:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"449088c5-9cbd-40e4-950a-1e34ecf3fc77"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Graph\>\"", "[", 
     RowBox[{"CycleGraph", "[", "5", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
  "[", "\"\<TableauForm\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[151]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"d225f4c9-ae5d-4897-8a97-c31a0e561588"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The display is the sign column beside a ten-by-ten binary grid, dividers \
separating the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d011847-970e-45d7-a13f-8153b260d4a5"],
 " bits from the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b737af00-3391-4e4e-bdd1-0b1c3f2ddc4f"],
 " bits and the destabilizer rows from the stabilizer rows; the stabilizer \
rows are the five ring generators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"]], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["w", "TI"], "\[Tilde]", 
     StyleBox["v", "TI"]}],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["w", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "967e4c43-3bc6-4c1e-8c0d-3952201aac8f"],
 ", so the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3049151a-6fcc-4827-9a15-706fb30e71b3"],
 " block is literally the adjacency matrix of the cycle while the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e0d23578-6aa0-4f5b-ae9d-1466cae48fba"],
 " block is the identity. This view is the algebra itself: the entanglement \
geometry of the ring is drawn in the binary pattern, and a Clifford gate acts \
by rewriting a few columns of this grid."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7e23be7d-8888-41b9-80df-ab14760f5019"],

Cell["The circuit, and the network behind it", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"59923bc1-75a2-4ff3-bc96-575bc1b0aa83"],

Cell["\<\
A circuit draws itself as a gate diagram. Take quantum phase estimation, the \
subroutine inside Shor's factoring and the HHL linear solver, on three \
counting qubits:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7626bc88-afdf-4739-83ce-f3d820abd0c3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qpe", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<PhaseEstimation\>\"", "[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[152]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"e26054e6-2f09-4cfd-970c-a93d4ae094b7"],

Cell["Draw it as a gate diagram:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5f6e0320-82a8-49ca-8fa8-5e83715f8c6f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qpe", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[153]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6dd4c61c-e7a1-40cb-9a2c-6205045a7ac1"],

Cell["\<\
The wire-and-gate picture lays out the algorithm: Hadamards on the counting \
register, the controlled powers of the unitary, and the inverse Fourier \
transform that reads the phase back. The same object also draws its internal \
structure, the tensor network that the engine contracts:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7632f310-5636-41d2-859b-a1afaf585aca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qpe", "[", "\"\<TensorNetworkGraph\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[154]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"60fa000c-51bc-46f9-9e5e-2bf0d858056a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 Cell[BoxData["Graph"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aafae04-88f1-4c3a-8518-ea261354e91c"],
 " whose vertices are the gate and state tensors and whose edges are the \
contracted indices: the diagram shows the physics, the network shows the \
computation, and Claim 4 steered the order in which such a network is \
contracted."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a39ad2fe-9a08-41d2-9901-bef747f68f7d"],

Cell["\<\
The same network renders in the dual picture too, as a hypergraph in which \
the roles swap, every index a vertex and every tensor one hyperedge spanning \
its indices:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36e05a26-0011-497d-850b-94e14ab6825e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qpe", "[", "\"\<TensorNetwork\>\"", "]"}], 
  "[", "\"\<Hypergraph\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[155]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"093391eb-706f-4290-9938-12b65183ce42"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["Hypergraph"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e92e9a1-ea16-4971-9f90-39c74a2e1aa2"],
 " with one hyperedge per tensor of the phase-estimation circuit, drawn over \
the network's indices: the tensor-contraction picture of the algorithm, in \
which contracting two tensors is the merging of two hyperedges."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f3247bb3-8b51-4b16-8333-2b8bf6f49766"],

Cell["Claim 7: An interoperability hub, down to real hardware", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7f5fce59-f08d-4c19-b070-53e115eb1247"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Key feature:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " the objects so far stayed inside QF; this claim sends them out. A QF \
object can leave QF for the rest of the quantum ecosystem, and foreign \
circuits can enter it; ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumQASM"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "28ccc060-cfb6-4aa4-bd88-44585be84787"],
 " is the single OpenQASM interface, and it runs in pure Wolfram Language \
with no external account. Each step below extends the interface: text export, \
foreign import, device-aware transpilation, and finally a physical quantum \
processor."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b9ff6c4c-c3bd-42db-82d9-37ae66557aea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Closest competitor.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Posting OpenQASM to a hardware provider is not itself unusual, MATLAB has \
submitted circuits to IBM Python-free since R2023b; the defensible part here \
is that device-native ISA transpilation runs in Wolfram Language and the same \
symbolic objects leave and re-enter the framework unchanged."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"219f0cb3-d7b1-46a0-b520-ebf10b7f40e5"],

Cell["Export to OpenQASM 3.0 (native, no Python)", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ee1e37de-db4d-4e48-9245-afb9e5ae38ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumQASM"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e78d8de6-0857-4df7-bbab-7be28d8a13ab"],
 " turns a circuit into the standard text format read by Qiskit, Cirq, and \
most hardware stacks."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"22aab548-1836-4742-9bd8-d1b6c7b30511"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"QuantumQASM", "[", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", "\"\<Toffoli\>\"", "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[156]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"cb7c43e0-c722-4516-9f9d-c43e100c9227"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The output is a complete OpenQASM 3.0 program for the three-qubit Toffoli \
gate: rather than a single ",
 Cell[BoxData["ccx"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "692f6f8b-e128-49bd-8d80-a35a40843424"],
 " instruction, the emitter writes the standard Clifford+",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71fe7318-81a8-44cf-82dc-f64533027318"],
 " decomposition, six CNOTs (each a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"ctrl", " ", "@", " ", "U"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bfab8dc1-ad26-43b8-89fa-d919986dd595"],
 ") interleaved with the non-Clifford ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b64663e-bf69-4ea9-84d3-2a62a13a16a9"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f1756c9a-5f51-4f81-99f5-e29ee5ac26ec"],
 " phases and a pair of Hadamards bracketing the target, every gate a \
concrete ",
 Cell[BoxData["U"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c65c750d-ed28-4427-b400-0be8a3d6cb7f"],
 " rotation. The native emitter writes OpenQASM 3.0, and the importer below \
reads OpenQASM 2.0 or 3.0 alike. A 2.0 export is available through the qiskit \
path, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumQASM", "[", 
   RowBox[{"circuit", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Version\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "2"}]}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d9476917-d155-4b65-bca0-75a4a4641f0d"],
 " (that route needs Python; the 3.0 export and all imports do not). Export \
needs concrete angles: a circuit with a symbolic parameter returns a ",
 Cell[BoxData["Failure"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a329f0a-01e3-44dd-a8f6-0e5d37c0e07c"],
 " rather than a QASM string, so resolve parameters to numbers at this \
boundary while keeping them symbolic everywhere else in QF (Claims 1 and 5)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b611fb41-f055-4fee-a1d6-1ef4e66712b7"],

Cell["\<\
Import foreign OpenQASM and compute with it (native, no Python)\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"2dfdbd80-5e9b-4403-b09b-96987e36004e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same interface runs the other way: give ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumCircuitOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0679c837-1cbf-4aff-bce4-99f761734666"],
 " an OpenQASM string authored anywhere and get back a QF circuit, parsed in \
pure WL, including ",
 Cell[BoxData["reset"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07f91b8d-9668-42eb-9116-2236e1a80f26"],
 ", controlled gates, and mid-circuit ",
 Cell[BoxData["measure"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a53baa62-37da-4bf0-8638-1685c6832825"],
 ". The importer reads each gate's angle as a Wolfram Language expression, so \
the angles can stay symbolic: write ",
 Cell["Pi/2", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "fd12258e-e252-40e5-8c84-4c58c2e90fce"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["Pi"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ae7f77c4-06cc-44ef-99c9-0e8b461c6cb9"],
 ", the exact constant, in place of their decimal expansions, and the \
imported circuit is exact rather than a floating-point copy. Import a \
four-qubit circuit that runs the optimal quantum strategy for the CHSH game:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f4238541-912d-4e49-8669-0c70453ae7c2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"chsh", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
  "QuantumCircuitOperator", 
   "[", "\"\<OPENQASM 3.0;\nqubit[4] q;\nbit[4] c;\nreset q[0];\nreset q[3];\n\
U(Pi/2, 0, Pi) q[3];\nU(Pi/2, 0, Pi) q[0];\nswap q[0] q[3];\nctrl(0) @ \
negctrl(1) @ U(Pi/2, Pi, Pi) q[0] q[3];\nctrl(1) @ negctrl(0) @ U(Pi/2, 0, 0) \
q[0] q[3];\nreset q[1];\nU(Pi/2, 0, Pi) q[1];\nreset q[2];\nU(Pi/2, 0, Pi) \
q[2];\nU(0, 0, 0) q[0];\nctrl(1) @ negctrl(0) @ U(Pi/2, 0, Pi) q[1] q[0];\n\
U(Pi/4, 0, 0) q[3];\nctrl(0) @ negctrl(1) @ U(Pi/2, 0, Pi) q[2] q[3];\nc[0] = \
measure q[0];\nc[1] = measure q[1];\nc[2] = measure q[2];\nc[3] = measure \
q[3];\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[157]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"755147fb-8d80-4a4f-8832-b45942ab9e3b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Note that QF reads ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"U", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "Pi"}], ")"}]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d9cbb122-523e-4aa2-91a5-37d4ceb82850"],
 ": the angle is the Wolfram constant ",
 Cell[BoxData["Pi"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9f76315a-f745-402b-ac51-13fdd953ab83"],
 ". A spec-strict OpenQASM 3 parser like qiskit knows only the lowercase ",
 Cell[BoxData["pi"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0823f082-d10b-4bc5-8de9-fbc7b378d72b"],
 " and rejects ",
 Cell[BoxData["Pi"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "267515ab-fe2a-44e7-89bb-b1b93871a64d"],
 " as an undefined symbol."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3da16b67-e2d4-4727-9ebb-f8578597263a"],

Cell["\<\
Once imported it is an ordinary QF object, exact end to end because every \
angle stayed a symbol.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7e8d0454-d3e4-4a98-af53-655ec1ee5c13"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the CHSH game the players win when their answers satisfy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[Wedge]", 
   StyleBox["y", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[CirclePlus]", 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "91170df9-161c-4e01-bfc8-f4f8078c738a"],
 ", and no classical strategy wins more than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["3", "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ac4f942-0596-4aa1-a25e-5c2e27956408"],
 " of the time; entanglement beats that bound. Read the circuit's joint \
measurement distribution, label the four outcomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00e2ed42-f091-49b0-ad60-fc533f45002a"],
 ", and ask Wolfram Language for the winning probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Pr",
   FontSlant->"Plain"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3140af90-d45d-45af-ac06-3c0b866aba8d"],
 ", in closed form:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3b3ade95-59dc-4977-9fac-7b0005f858fa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Probability", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"BitAnd", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
     RowBox[{"BitXor", "[", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "b"}], "}"}], " ", 
     "\[Distributed]", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"chsh", "[", "]"}], "[", "\"\<MultivariateDistribution\>\"", 
      "]"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "//", " ", "FullSimplify"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[158]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"263988a5-2bef-467e-83f5-7f2c6e2b2f1c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Because the angles never left exact arithmetic, the winning probability \
returns as a closed form, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"2", "+", 
     SqrtBox["2"]}], "4"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "8"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5cb98408-d0c4-47f6-8d83-e72cab407783"],
 ", exactly the Tsirelson bound, the quantum maximum for CHSH and the \
algebraic number a sampled estimate only converges toward. A circuit authored \
in another tool became an exact probability read off with native WL \
statistics."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"579b5719-7753-4a2a-9f7a-487954a29e22"],

Cell["A hardware-aware transpilation target", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"fcc44775-1f38-45fe-a55f-4d457e4ef9bf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["QiskitTarget"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ae1a4b29-bf8a-492b-9458-45ea1fe85d60"],
 " carries a device spec (qubit count, native gate set, connectivity), \
validated at construction against qiskit's own ",
 Cell[BoxData["Target"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9257788e-73f7-440f-a4d4-e241d6a67455"],
 " schema through the Python bridge. Build a 5-qubit linear-chain device:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f5adcf36-3bef-425b-8523-9e24bdb2005d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"target", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QiskitTarget", "[", 
   RowBox[{"<|", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<NumQubits\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "5"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<BasisGates\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<cx\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<rz\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<sx\>\"", ",",
         " ", "\"\<x\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<CouplingMap\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "|>"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[159]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"64166e0e-7910-40ab-9ce2-8fe6a4d4ad30"],

Cell["Read its coupling map back:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c713f201-7e39-4d46-8bf6-d1c41d06ae09"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"target", "[", "\"\<CouplingMap\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[160]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"c5fa795d-abe1-4288-bd78-ab164492a69b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Pass the target to ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumQASM"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e14696d3-da7d-413d-86e2-19c1852d7a3b"],
 " as an option, and the circuit is transpiled to that backend's native gates \
and connectivity:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"632fb8c6-37de-4b4b-9cdd-a5fbcfeef712"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"QuantumQASM", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Fourier\>\"", "[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Target\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "target"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[161]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"b40a0c15-a499-46c3-9f4b-c1347dc2b414"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The QFT comes back rewritten for the device: its controlled-phase rotations \
decomposed into the native ",
 Cell[BoxData["rz"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a33387e0-b22a-4e01-b2a9-3291e5fe4150"],
 "/",
 Cell[BoxData["sx"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a9a89f8-ae7e-44d5-adad-665276e89746"],
 "/",
 Cell[BoxData["x"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e45e8a96-c502-45a7-8844-88274bf046da"],
 " set, the entangling steps as ",
 Cell[BoxData["cx"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "caa5910b-41d1-434a-afe9-fdce9f2dc310"],
 " on physical qubits, every two-qubit gate routed along an edge the coupling \
map allows. Transpiling a Fourier transform, with its all-to-all controlled \
phases, is a realistic instance of this task, where both decomposition and \
routing are non-trivial."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2c7be4b0-804d-4277-a9ac-0e256a97ad05"],

Cell["Submit to a real IBM QPU, and compare to the exact result", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"596d1538-8402-4371-80bf-b5ded875e17d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An IBM account connects through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"ServiceConnect", "[", "\"\<IBMQuantumPlatform\>\"", "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9b85a8f2-ddd0-4b69-8d69-ec3959295d7f"],
 ", after which ",
 Cell[BoxData["IBMJobSubmit"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b7a59410-918a-4f70-990d-cd987b6eeaf7"],
 " sends a circuit to the hardware asynchronously and returns an ",
 Cell[BoxData["IBMJob"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c3f68d7-a7a3-4099-87e2-b70f62d6c16c"],
 " handle. Create an API key and copy your instance's cloud resource name \
(CRN) from your IBM Quantum Platform account, then connect, the placeholder \
",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<xxx\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "81147280-c49d-4f99-94b8-e5d932a4ddf3"],
 " values standing in for your own:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"58d1e23f-63b8-460d-ba8b-4f97eda7dfb8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"api", " ", "=", " ", "\"\<xxx\>\""}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"LocalSymbol", "[", "\"\<ibm_crn\>\"", "]"}], " ", "=", 
   " ", "\"\<xxx\>\""}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ServiceConnect", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<IBMQuantumPlatform\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<New\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Authentication", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<apikey\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "api"}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[162]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"483d00bb-f9d3-47a1-bfa9-ea8e8e1c3339"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The call returns a ",
 Cell[BoxData["ServiceObject"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "edf061fb-4247-436c-bd57-ce1e57eab5c8"],
 " connection handle. A QPU job needs a circuit that ends in a measurement; \
in QF a list of qubit indices placed in the circuit is exactly that, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dbe51be7-4332-4cbd-822a-1ff677790354"],
 " measures all three qubits. Build the measured GHZ circuit:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bde78161-e30d-45be-956a-19e8b8b4261a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ghz", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<GHZ\>\"", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[163]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4894bdd4-f0fa-4536-930f-e0811e76fd70"],

Cell["\<\
Submit it to the backend, which returns a handle immediately:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4aa58a61-0907-42e2-a530-239b63900770"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"job", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"IBMJobSubmit", "[", 
   RowBox[{"ghz", ",", " ", "\"\<ibm_fez\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Shots\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "4096"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[164]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"f117fbf3-1daf-416e-9433-44ee133090aa"],

Cell["Check the status:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b82de55d-797c-45e8-b988-920af048e403"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"job", "[", "\"\<Status\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[165]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"26818326-1b9b-4f55-a7c1-4baa0f0aa58b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The handle returns immediately with status ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Queued\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bbacf557-e3d8-430d-87da-e12350020d14"],
 " while the job waits in the device queue. The same circuit runs exactly in \
the Wolfram Language by applying it:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0428a888-3022-491c-94b1-2a570d585ee7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"wl", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ghz", "[", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[166]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"bf5bd08a-992b-48e3-ae01-3167eeb90dae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cbb0e742-2e26-4355-b0c6-2a11ee9033dc"],
 " with probabilities ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4496da5f-c0d8-46f0-af13-473747bf6cd6"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData["000"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a68759a-727d-414c-a20b-b7a550f6010f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6edc4967-2b68-4c46-93c2-49b8f086e140"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData["111"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c9670545-d5db-47fa-908a-0f5ca66aacfe"],
 ". Once the job completes, the hardware outcome comes back as the same kind \
of ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b5c45529-9037-4628-828f-d1ce17067f11"],
 " object, decoded into the same qubit order:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b87c728-a2d5-4935-92cf-c62368dc42f0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qpu", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"job", "[", "\"\<Refresh\>\"", "]"}], "[", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[167]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"d58fc63a-c678-41c1-a427-79463dfeeebc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This run returned ",
 Cell[BoxData["4096"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41edd5f2-3e67-46a0-b532-dac33548e5c7"],
 " shots from ",
 Cell[BoxData["ibm_fez"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54c2afcb-e79e-4f6a-ab77-29c6bebaf70d"],
 ". Because the two results are the same kind of object, hardware noise can \
be shown in one chart, the exact and measured probabilities paired per basis \
state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8438e35e-672e-4240-b6d4-d2027b4de561"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"BarChart", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Values", " ", "@*", " ", "KeySort"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"wl", "[", "\"\<Probabilities\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"qpu", "[", "\"\<Probabilities\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",",
    "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ChartLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Exact WL\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<QPU\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLabels", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Keys", "[", 
     RowBox[{"wl", "[", "\"\<Probabilities\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[168]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"edc370c3-6855-4151-8d49-c1274477b495"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The exact bars are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e040123-ffab-4d97-bb55-3eaf729b30b7"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData["000"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cecad02-82f1-4fa0-b856-248eae7038c9"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["111"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cac5335-6705-4860-b817-03176e6f44d8"],
 " and zero elsewhere; the device's two tall bars fall visibly short of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23dee55c-39b9-4363-a754-3a62660774f7"],
 ", with the missing weight spread thinly over the six bitstrings the exact \
state forbids. That gap, read bar by bar from one figure, is the device noise."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d6d34fd5-4265-4ca0-911f-66abeb19fa3d"],

Cell["Where This Stops", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a9f94a19-c3b3-4908-9386-4b9f4f48e397"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every closed form in this document rests on one fact, and so does its \
limit: a symbolic result exists exactly as far as the underlying spectrum is \
solvable in radicals. The eigenvalues of a matrix up to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", "\[Times]", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0dbde658-e914-4dfd-9d50-a8a8f684830d"],
 " are closed-form (radicals reach through the quartic); at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"5", "\[Times]", "5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3668d3a9-da43-4da6-a438-c3ec96a485d8"],
 " and beyond they are generically ",
 Cell[BoxData["Root"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a525780-0f8c-4927-a965-0a44a1c86fdc"],
 " objects with no elementary form, by Abel-Ruffini. That algebraic boundary, \
not the qubit count, is where the symbolic path ends."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c28a4cf3-0248-4448-8742-ff721e0b260e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two of the results above sit at this boundary. The many-body entanglement \
entropy of Claim 1 is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "1"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["log",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "1"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aaa00565-5905-4bb4-bf7a-2167df94b586"],
 ", a function of the eigenvalues of the reduced density matrix; it stays a \
formula while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07f0ee0c-f2dc-4a0c-969a-6c850a48b7bf"],
 " is at most ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", "\[Times]", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d783eedc-c700-4a29-ad74-89b02ce55dfb"],
 ", and once a larger block is traced out those eigenvalues become quintic \
roots and the entropy loses its closed form. The master equation of Claim 2 \
solves symbolically only when the Liouvillian's spectrum is solvable: the \
structured relaxation there returns a closed form at once, but a generically \
driven open system, whose secular determinant is a high-degree or \
unstructured polynomial, returns an unwieldy radical expression or nothing in \
workable time."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9a9fd36a-5740-4ec9-ac40-2abba98c213c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So the scope is narrow and exact. QF carries a computation to closed form \
precisely when the physics has a closed-form spectrum, and it indicates the \
limit by returning a ",
 Cell[BoxData["Root"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a3d553d-5680-4567-b513-36745561e1c2"],
 " object the moment that fails, rather than a wrong answer or a silent \
truncation. The symbolic path is deep, not wide: it runs as far as the \
algebra allows and stops at the boundary set by Abel and Ruffini. Beyond that \
boundary the same objects still compute, now numerically, which is why every \
claim above also has a purely numeric reading."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c8f1b219-f6dd-483f-a349-da46baa09781"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"71476510-c6db-4859-a564-968b03d6631b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Seven claims, each demonstrated in executed code. Symbolic algebra carried \
dynamics to closed form: the Rabi propagator of a rotating drive, a \
Landau-Zener sweep expressed in parabolic cylinder functions, a QAOA \
landscape whose exact maximum is a closed-form cubic root, the entanglement \
entropy of a quench as a function of time. One object model held the rest of \
the theory: channels, POVMs, Fock space, and phase space; a master equation \
solved once for every initial state and every rate, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], "\[LessEqual]", "2", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "660ebbd6-da4a-43dc-a775-31b4eb83a2a2"],
 " arriving as a theorem rather than a remembered rule; a basis and a \
dimension on every object, a spin-1 Hamiltonian and a five-site ring each \
diagonalized by its own named basis; a state reconstructed from measured \
counts at a fidelity close to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6413be94-c6f8-447c-88b6-4c5aabf7d561"],
 ". Measurement stayed inside the physics: records became quantum wires, \
teleportation carried its classical channel as a quantum wire, a coherent \
error was digitized and corrected at codeword fidelity exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a594a007-2a39-4094-8c64-8565a0d47774"],
 ", and a measurement ran backwards. Underneath, three engines computed the \
same objects: exact state-vector algebra, a steered tensor-network \
contraction, and a stabilizer tableau that carried a thousand qubits to \
near-maximal half-chain entanglement computed exactly, the representations \
converting into one another exactly. Because these objects are ordinary \
Wolfram Language expressions, the kernel's own functions transformed them \
directly, exponentiating a generator into its propagator and differentiating \
a gate to recover the Hamiltonian that drives it, and each of them drew \
itself. And the same objects left the system: out to OpenQASM and back, \
through a transpiler to a device's native gates, and onto a physical quantum \
processor, whose ",
 Cell[BoxData["4096"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fc4d20a-f58d-49d6-948b-52b891cb4785"],
 "-shot histogram stands in this document next to the exact distribution it \
approximates."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"89d17849-f4d1-4a2c-ac5b-1bcfe93117f3"],

Cell["\<\
Behind all seven claims is one mechanism: quantum objects that are exact \
symbolic expressions compose, with each other and with the entire language. \
One consequence ran through every example: the result was exact, the \
algebraic QAOA optimum, the closed-form relaxation law, the integer \
stabilizer entropy, the exactly-recovered teleported state, never a value \
sampled near the answer but the exact quantity such a sample converges \
toward. That is the numerical claim underlying the symbolic one: where a \
numeric simulation or a finite measurement returns an estimate, QF returns \
the exact object it estimates. The distance from writing a Hamiltonian to \
reading its closed form, or to running it on hardware, is a few composable \
calls. A result that is a formula can be differentiated, reduced, or taken to \
a limit; a result that is a circuit is already in the format the rest of the \
quantum ecosystem uses.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e43377ee-5a3f-4f99-ad67-8a07a074acaf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The next steps are the reader's: change the graph under the QAOA section, \
raise the spin past ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66d664da-31aa-4bba-a7f8-e40072fd2565"],
 ", swap damping for dephasing, tilt the repetition code's coherent error off \
the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a6c99cd-08bc-4be8-9c23-63dfe81f620c"],
 " axis, point the last section at a different backend. The document \
re-derives itself."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00ed0bae-6203-44a7-9ebb-315b10df5a37"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Setup.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Evaluate once before the cells; this installs the development builds of \
the QuantumFramework and TensorNetworks paclets and loads them:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aaf3504b-8acb-47d5-a25e-66d0dabe0d65"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"PacletInstall", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<https://www.wolfr.am/DevWQCF\>\"", ",", " ", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ForceVersionInstall", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"", "]"}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"PacletInstall", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<https://www.wolfr.am/DevWTN\>\"", ",", " ", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ForceVersionInstall", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`TensorNetworks`\>\"", "]"}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[169]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4da13a07-4248-4ef8-992c-9d41146c5c74"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every cell was executed as shown (Wolfram Language 15.0, ",
 Cell["Wolfram/QuantumFramework", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "29181ce6-0a46-4e54-8fe7-989f2b4f521d"],
 " 2.0.0) and every stated output is the captured result, including the \
hardware run on ",
 Cell[BoxData["ibm_fez"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69bfae6e-b27d-41dc-929a-ea49acc9bfff"],
 "; reproducing the transpilation cells needs a Python installation with \
qiskit, and the hardware cells an IBM Quantum account."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"552d8e6c-35d6-4df0-ad1e-8fffecd31a50"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Taken together, these features, and above all the way symbolic algebra, \
numerical simulation, and visualization live inside one object, make QF a \
particularly effective tool for teaching and learning quantum theory at every \
level, from a first qubit to graduate research: a student can build a state, \
evolve it, draw it, and read its closed form in a single expression, the \
computation-first habit this document follows throughout. Wolfram develops \
that direction directly, in the book ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Quantum Computing by Model and Simulation: A \
Computational Approach",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://www.wolfram-media.com/products/quantum-computing-by-model-\
and-simulation/"], None}], "TI"],
 " (Wolfram Media), which teaches the subject through modeling and simulation \
in the framework, and in ",
 ButtonBox["Wolfram U",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://www.wolfram.com/wolfram-u/"], None}],
 ", whose free interactive courses and study groups include quantum computing \
and related topics."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9bfe79f9-a9ea-444e-a002-49a46c2e7622"]
},
CreateCellID->True,
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (February 17, 2026)",
